    (0x43EB20, 0x2, 'shared-mutable', '0x65CD0: for a printable key (0x20 < k < 0x7F, 0x65CDB..0x65CE3) it writes the char at 0x43EB20 (0x65CE5) and NUL at 0x43EB21 (0x65CEB) and returns 0x43EB20 (0x65CF2); other keys return table strings. Key subsystem scratch return buffer. [review 0]'),
    (0x45279C, 0x530, 'shared-mutable', 'every player-role writer is a GL entry point. 0x73290 fills the GL table 0x6A84C8.. with 0x6FF60 (glBegin, stored at 0x73411/0x73416), 0x70050, 0x70260, 0x702D0, 0x70370, 0x70430, 0x704C0, 0x70550, 0x70670, 0x70870, 0x70C20, 0x70EE0, 0x712B0, 0x71920, 0x71950, 0x71D40, 0x71D90, 0x71E00, 0x71EC0 (all in the 0x733xx..0x745xx stores). 0x73030 is glSelectTexture (0x7479C stores it in [0x5519AC]); 0x6F080/0x6F550/0x6F910/0x725E0 are its helpers. Start-up 0x720E0 initialises the block (the rep movsd into 0x452870 and 0x452C70). One GL state for the one device. The extent is the cluster span; it does not matter for a shared object. [review 0]'),
    (0x452E10, None, 'shared-mutable', 'written only by 0x71950, a GL table entry (stored by 0x73290 at 0x74587), at [idx+0x452E10..0x452E20]. The 0x2C stride shows at 0x14718 (imul ecx,0x2C; [ecx+0x452E24] at 0x1471F). GL texture objects of the one context. [review 0]'),
    (0x49EDFC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'written by the GL entries 0x71D90, 0x71E00, 0x71EC0 (stored by 0x73290) and 0x71D40 (glVertex2f, FINDINGS.md); start-up 0x720E0 initialises it. The loading screen draw 0xC2BC0 goes through the same GL layer. [review 0]'),
    (0x49F67C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the particle allocator: 0x87040 pops the free head [0x49F688] (0x87041..0x87053) and pushes onto the active head [0x49F67C] (0x8704D..0x87069). 0x87970 frees an entity\'s particles back (0x87A1D..0x87A48, 0x87A7A). R_DrawParticles 0x89C60 (from the render 0x865D0) moves them (0x89CE4/0x89CEA). R_ClearParticles 0x830F0 (R_NewMap) relinks them from the one pool pointer [0x49F680], allocated at start-up by 0x82EB0 ("-particles", 0x82EA1). The heads link nodes of one shared pool, so swapping them per player without a per-player pool would corrupt the lists. Behaviour note: player 2\'s effects add particles that player 1 draws. [review 0]'),
    (0x49F688, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the free-list head of the same pool (see above). [review 0]'),
    (0x4DF174, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', '0x15400/0x15540 set 3 (0x15412, 0x15559) and 0x159F0 restores it from [0x4DF170] (0x15B7E..0x15B91), next to the device state saves of [14]. Start-up 0x93F70 (vertex shaders) sets the same values (0x93F73). [review 0]'),
    (0x4DF184, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the same pattern: 0x15434/0x15577 set 4, 0x159F0 restores it from [0x4DF180] (0x15B97..0x15BA9), start-up 0x93FB5. [review 0]'),
    (0x5266E0, None, 'shared-mutable', '0xC2860 (called from 0xC37E0, the "playermodels.txt" loader) strcpys the token from a stack buffer into 0x5266E0 (0xC28D1..0xC28E0). Nothing in the code reads 0x5266E0 (the only reference is 0xC28D7). A write-only scratch copy, written while loading (0xC3E90, which also steps the load progress [6]). Its extent cannot be proven: an unbounded strcpy from a 0x40C-byte stack frame. [review 0]'),
    (0x526BE8, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer scratch: GL_LoadTexture 0x48880 strcpy of the identifier into it (0x488D8..0x488E9, loop to NUL; same loop in GL_BuildLightmaps 0x52D75..0x52D82 and R_LoadSkys 0x58060..0x5806D); read back only as a %s argument (push 0x526BE8 at 0xC34FC/0xC35AB/0xC365B, 0x72984..). Rewritten before each use, one GL context; only player 1 draws in M2. Extent not proven (unbounded strcpy); shared, so no extent needed [review 32]'),
    (0x527288, 0x1F4, 'shared-mutable', 'voice/sound: 0x103430 checks index 0..4 (cmp edi,5 at 0x103437), stride 0x64 (imul 0x64 at 0x10343C), base lea 0x527288 at 0x103440, names the slot "?VoiceData" and starts it with S_StartDynamicSound 0x100F10 (call 0x103493). 5 x 0x64. Sound is one copy for the process; M2 added player starts no sound [review 32]'),
    (0x537B40, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'scratch: 0x149F10 (client COM_Parse) writes the token ([edx+0x537B40] at 0x149F6C/0x149FA3, NUL at 0x149F7C/0x149FD0, single char at 0x149FD8/0x149FDE); its only consumer 0x1A7D80 (rumble script parser) reads it right after each call (push 0x537B40 at 0x1A7DB7..0x1A7E65). Fully rewritten before each use within one call. Extent unbounded (no length check), not needed for shared [review 32]'),
    (0x5430D8, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'three string pointers of the map media loader 0xC3E90 (called by SV_SpawnServer 0x9FEF0 and CL_ParseServerInfo 0x2E780): freed and zeroed by the loop 0xC3F77..0xC3F98 (esi from 0x5430D8 to <0x5430E4, step 4); set by 0xC37E0 (0xC3809, 0xC39C2/0xC3A95, 0xC39F2/0xC3AE8) from the map name 0x55209C; consumed by the server game precache (0x140FB0 at 0x141B88). One map / one server: shared [review 32]'),
    (0x5430E8, 0x1E0, 'process', 'Initialize 0x18B7A0 copies 0x78 dwords (mov ecx,0x78 at 0x18B7A8, rep movsd at 0x18B7B2 and again 0x18B7C0) from the engine-supplied table: the engine functions, the same for every player; called through by the client and the server game (call [0x543148]..) [review 32]'),
    (0x543360, 0x80, 'process', 'extent: the loop in 0x18E430 runs esi from 0x543360 (0x18F08E) step 4 (0x18F25A) to <0x5433E0 (0x18F260): 32 dwords. Written only by HUD_PrepEntity 0x18D550 (mov [eax*4+0x543360],ebx at 0x18D5D2) with ebx = a fixed static weapon object (0x3A1378, 0x3A14E0, ... at 0x18E26F..) and index from its own ItemInfo: the same pointer values for every player and every call; the per-player state is in the pointed-to objects, not here [review 32]'),
    (0x54369C, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 access [esi],[esi+4],[esi+8] (0x18F842..0x18F868, 0x18F897..0x18F8DD) with esi=0x54369C (IN_UseDown 0x18FD82, IN_UseUp 0x18FDA1); 0x190400 writes all three (0x19048C/0x190492/0x190486). Input state of the client game, each local client its own (the added player reads no pad, so its copy must not see player 1''s buttons) [review 32]"),
    (0x5439B8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the pad-to-key bridge 0x19DFD0 builds the button mask from the physical pad 0x384F9C + 0xE0*[0x3852F8] (0x19DFD0..0x19E05E), posts key events through [0x5431A8] (0x19E131) and stores the mask (0x19E149). Also called by the Xbox UI (0xC6F70, 0xC7330, 0xE19C0, 0xE9320). It follows the one physical pad, which only player 1 reads in M2; IN_Init 0x19DF43 clears it. Revisit when each player gets its own pad [review 32]'),
    (0x543A04, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the loop bound of 0x19DFD0 (cmp esi,eax at 0x19E13A..0x19E140); set to constants only (8 by IN_Init at 0x19DF25, 16 by 0x19DFD0 at 0x19E067); belongs to the same shared pad bridge [review 32]'),
    (0x543A94, 0x18, 'player', "two vec3: 0x1A0600 copies 0x543A94..0x543A9C to [esi] and 0x543AA0..0x543AA8 to [edi] (0x1A0604..0x1A0633); the player-movement code 0x1A3740 copies both into the pmove (0x1A376B..0x1A379B) under iJumpSpectator 0x5D8EBC; written by the spectator code (DirectorMessage 0x1A8DB5..0x1A8DEC, FindNextPlayer 0x1A9104.., FindPlayer 0x1A928B.., SetSpectatorStartPosition 0x1A87DA..). The client''s own spectator camera [review 32]"),
    (0x5456D0, 0x288, 'process', 'rep stosd of 0xA2 dwords (mov ecx,0xA2 at 0x1A585D, edi 0x5456D0 at 0x1A5862, 0x1A5867), then filled by loops whose values come only from constants (0x365E98, 0x365E90, 0x365E88, 0x3F800000, 0x40C00000; 0x1A5880..0x1A5A41): the same contents every time it is built; read by 0x1A33F0 [review 32]'),
    (0x545A68, 0x4, 'player', "written by the client weapon''s SendWeaponAnim 0x18D840 (0x18D868, under g_runfuncs 0x552C68) and by HUD_WeaponsPostThink 0x18E430 (cmp at 0x18F06B, write 0x18F076) before calling pfnWeaponAnim [0x5431F0]. The predicted view-model animation of this client [review 32]"),
    (0x548720, 0x4, 'player', "shots-fired counter: incremented by the client''s own fire events (EV_Fire* 0x1E36B0 at 0x1E3835/0x1E383E, 0x1E7B10, 0x1E99D0, 0x1EA500, ...), read and clamped by the crosshair draw 0x1AD3B0 (0x1AD568, 0x1AD5C7..0x1AD5D4). Dword accesses only [review 32]"),
    (0x548744, 0x4, 'player', 'g_iUser2: set from the local player state by 0x18C5E0 (0x18C758), by the spectator code (0x1A9000, 0x1A91B0, 0x1A9480 at 0x1A9551, DirectorMessage 0x1A8D51), reset by CHudSpectator 0x1AA9F0 (0x1AAA35) [review 32]'),
    (0x548748, 0x4, 'player', "g_iUser1 (observer mode): 0x18C5E0 (0x18C73A), 0x1A9480 (0x1A957E..0x1A96EF), 0x1AA9F0 (0x1AAA3B); read by the client''s view/HUD code [review 32]"),
    (0x548E74, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'vec3 passed by pointer to the triangle API Fog (push 0x548E74 at 0x18F5BD, call [eax+0x34] at 0x18F5C2); its only writer is the reset 0x1CC5D0, which stores constant 0 into its three dwords (0x1CC5E1, 0x1CC5EB, 0x1CC5F5): the same value always. Not protected: 0x1CC5D0 (the fog reset, called by 0x1A5EE0 / 0x18B970 while playing) writes it [review 32]'),
    (0x548F3C, 0x10, 'shared-mutable', 'BEGIN_READ state: every HUD message handler writes all four before reading: e.g. 0x1A61B0 sets 0x548F3C=0 (0x1A61D9), 0x548F44=0 (0x1A61DF), 0x548F48=size (0x1A61E5), 0x548F40=buffer (0x1A61EB), then advances 0x548F3C/sets 0x548F44 on overrun (0x1A6213..0x1A6231); the same pattern in 0x1A5D80, 0x1A5E40, 0x1A5FC0, 0x1A60D0, 0x1A6260, 0x1CC733.., 0x1B5389... One message is read start to end within a call: scratch, the same rule as msg_readcount [review 32]'),
    (0x549148, 0x200, 'player', "g_szPrelocalisedMenuString: appended with strncat bounded by 0x200-strlen (0x1B5582..0x1B55AC, push 0x549148), the last byte 0x549347 forced to 0 (0x1B55B6, 0x1D7F96). Written by the ShowMenu handler 0x1A63F0 / 0x1D7E80: the client''s own HUD data [review 32]"),
    (0x549350, 0x200, 'player', "g_szMenuString: localised copy written byte by byte (0x1B55E0..0x1B55EF, 0x1D7FC0..0x1D7FCF, again 0x1B5614/0x1D7FF4); the draw loop 0x1D7C20 reads it with ecx < 0x200 (0x1D7CC3). The client''s HUD menu [review 32]"),
    (0x549770, 0x19, 'shared-mutable', 'scratch: 0x1F3BD0 writes the whole string byte by byte (0x1F3C86..0x1F3D2A, NUL at 0x549788; the digit at 0x549783 picked at 0x1F3D46..0x1F3D61), then passes it at once to the engine model loader (push 0x549770, call [ecx+0x0C] at 0x1F3D6E/0x1F3D73); rebuilt the same way at 0x1F40E8... Fully rewritten before each use [review 32]'),
    (0x551810, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: a texture-stage-setup flag set by 0x14380 (0x14419) after programming the D3D state cache 0x314A30..0x314A84 / 0x316FF0, cleared by 0x14430 (0x14515) and 0x14780 (0x147AE); also 0x197BD0 (BSPShader.vsh). One D3D device [review 32]'),
    (0x551814, 0x10, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: the saved D3D textures of 4 stages: 0x15400 writes [esi+0x551814] with esi 0..0xC step 4 (0x154D8, 0x15527..0x1552D cmp esi,0x10), 0x15540 restores them with esi < 4 (0x159C6..0x159D9, call 0x306460) [review 32]'),
    (0x551860, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'the demo facility\'s directory: its entry count 0x551860 and its entries 0x551864 (stride 0x5C, 1E6E1), one object: the record command 0x210D0 clears both with Q_memset(0x551860, 0, 8) (0x213C4..0x213D0, the same at 0x2130D), stores the count 2 (0x213DA) and allocates 0xB8 bytes (0x213D5..0x213E4); written by the demo console commands (appenddemo 0x1E2C0 at 0x1E70B, swapdemo 0x1E8E0, setdemoinfo 0x1EE20, removedemo 0x1F5B0, 0x20E30) and by CL_StopPlayback 0x20C70 (0x20CED) only when cls.demoplayback 0x785458 is set (0x20C7A). The added player plays no demo in M2. Was two entries (the count shared, the pointer a player\'s): the block write found by the Q_memset scan joins them [review 32, 2/ut_32; docs 15]'),
    (0x551870, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'the sprite list (SPR_*): list pointer 0x551870, count 0x551874, current sprite 0x551878. SPR_Init 0x1CAC0 allocates 0x80 entries of 0xC (count 0x80 at 0x1CAFE, 0x600 bytes, rep stosd 0x180 at 0x1CB14..0x1CB1B) only if the list is null (0x1CADB..0x1CAEC); SPR_Load 0x22B20 finds or adds by name; SPR_Shutdown 0x22C50 frees (stride 0xC at 0x22CA2). A name-keyed cache of shared models; the current sprite is set by SPR_Set 0x22E40 for drawing, and only player 1 draws [review 32]'),
    (0x551890, 0x4, 'player', 'cl_entities: allocated by CL_ReallocateDynamicData 0x2E2E0 as cl.max_edicts (0x749D40, in cl) x 0x74C (0x2E31F..0x2E34D), freed by 0x2E2A0 (0x2E2B5) and CL_Disconnect 0x28F20 (0x2906C); read across the client code. Each client its own entity array, sized from its own cl [review 32]'),
    (0x5518AC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "head of the user-message list (nodes of 0x20: next at +0x18, handler at +0x1C, name at +8): HookUserMsg 0x2C690 returns the existing node for the same name and handler (0x2C6F7..0x2C702), else adds one (0x2C70F.., 0x2C790); svc_newusermsg 0x31010 sets the ids (0x2C4B6/0x2C4B8, new node 0x2C4CB..0x2C4EE); freed by 0x1CA40 (0x1CA90..0x1CAA2). The handlers are the one client DLL''s functions and the ids come from the one server: identical for every player [review 32]"),
    (0x5518E8, 0x8, 'server', 'two arrays allocated by 0x3D040 (called by SV_SpawnServer 0x9FEF0 / 0xA00ED; 0x3D1DF, 0x3D1AE), indexed with the element size 0x4257F0 by the server code 0x3D000/0x3D020 (callers 0x96280) and 0x3CF30; freed by Host_ClearMemory 0x5CC60 (0x5CC88/0x5CC8E), which the client reaches only through CL_ClearState 0x28E60 when sv.active 0x5EF7C0 is 0 (0x28E60..0x28E6C), never in a listen server [review 32]'),
    (0x551998, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: set by R_RenderView 0x4EC60 (0x4ECEE / 0x4ECF6 / 0x4EDAC, between GL calls), read by the GL world/entity code (0x50420, 0x70070, 0x707B0, 0x70870) and by 0x93520 (0x93520). Only player 1 draws [review 32]'),
    (0x551CBC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the Xbox UI shell: set when an xbui dialog opens (ControllerUnplugged 0xC8330 at 0xC8403.., NetworkCableUnplugged 0xE9240, HostQuiting 0xE92C0, HostFull 0xE93A0, HighLatency 0xE9660 at 0xE961E, 0xF30C0), read by SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10 (0x55F99). One UI [review 32]'),
    (0x551CCC, 0x4, 'player', "start time of an engine screen message: 0x55230 copies two strings (to 0x6CE3E0 and 0x6CE460) and stores cl.time 0x74A290 (0x55255/0x5525B); called from the client game''s SayText/radio handler 0x1D8DF0. The draw 0x55790 compares it with cl.time and clears it (0x55796..0x557C5). Written with the client''s own message and its own cl.time. Its text buffers 0x6CE3E0/0x6CE460 need the same ownership (extent not checked here) [review 32]"),
    (0x551CD0, 0x4, 'player', 'the same for the second message: 0x55270 (strings to 0x6CE420 / 0x6CE300, cl.time at 0x5529B), cleared by 0x55790 (0x55804) [review 32]'),
    (0x551D88, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'double (fld/fstp qword): the running average of host_frametime 0x6CE0E0 updated by Host_Frame 0x5D2E0 (0x5D36C..0x5D38D), read by Host_GetHostInfo 0x5CF50 for the fps (0x5CF51..0x5CF85). Host statistics, one host [review 32]'),
    (0x551D98, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the spawn count the GL texture cache tags textures with (read by GL_LoadTexture 0x48880 at 0x48A2A/0x48B1B, 0x486F0 at 0x48718, 0x725E0 at 0x72722): set by SV_SpawnServer 0x9FEF0 from svs.spawncount (0xA000D..0xA0015) and by CL_ParseServerInfo 0x2E780 from cl.servercount (0x2EBC8/0x2EBCD), the same value from the one server. Renderer state [review 32]'),
    (0x551E0C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the network layer: head of the net_api request list (Net_SendRequest 0x67EF0 adds at 0x67FE0; 0x67E60 from CL_ReadPackets 0x28A40 expires against the host realtime 0x6CE040 and frees, 0x67E70..0x67EA5; 0x67E20; cleared by 0x67C40 and at start-up 0x2BA10) [review 32]'),
    (0x551E10, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the network layer: head of the parsed server list (NET_ParseServerList 0x68930 at 0x68C35; cleared by 0x67C70 / 0x2BA10) [review 32]'),
    (0x551E74, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: set by the map media loader 0xC3E90 (0xC3EEA), read by the texture upload 0x725E0 (0x72638) [review 32]'),
    (0x551E78, 0x34, 'shared-mutable', "the Xbox GL layer''s render-state bitmask: 13 dwords 0x551E78..0x551EA8 cleared together by 0x6EC50 (0x6EC52..0x6EC94); tested as a bit array by 0x6ECA0 (test [ecx*4+0x551E78], bit esi&0x1F, word esi>>5 at 0x6ECA9..0x6ECBA); written by the GL code (0x6EF60, 0x6F080, 0x70870, ...). One D3D device [review 32]"),
    (0x551EEC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer scratch: incremented by the add functions 0x93340 (from 0x4D0D0, called by R_RenderView 0x4EC60) and 0x93520 (guarded by the render flag 0x551998 at 0x93520..0x9352A; 0x9355E), drawn and reset to 0 by R_DrawTransEntities 0x93600 (0x93957). Built and emptied within one render pass; only player 1 draws [review 32]'),
    (0x551F98, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the input focus of the console and keyboard (values 0, 1, 4; "Bad key_dest" in 0x65ED0): written by console commands (0x5E7A0, 0x61450, 0x65ED0), the host (0x5E740, 0x5D5D0 at 0x5D65A), Sys_Error 0xAC090 (0xAC179), the demo timing 0x21F90, 0x64720. One console, one keyboard [review 32]'),
    (0x552030, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', "V_RenderView 0xB5E90 clears three dwords (0xB5EAA..0xB5EB6) and after rendering copies r_refdef.vieworg 0x6E7FD0..0x6E7FD8 into them (0xB61BF..0xB61DB); Host_Frame''s sound update 0x5D1E0 passes 0x552030 to 0xC59A0 (0x5D222/0x5D227). Rendering and sound: only player 1 draws and plays sound [review 32]"),
    (0x55209C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the current map name pointer, set by the map media loader 0xC3E90 (0xC3FF9) from SV_SpawnServer and CL_ParseServerInfo; read by the server game (0x119396, 0x11D06A), the Xbox shell (0xAD8A0) and the UI. One map [review 32]'),
    (0x5520A4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the loading screen: 0xC2FE0 ("levelloadscreen", 0xC3254/0xC325F), 0xC32E0 (0xC3300), SCR draw 0xB4560 (0xB4610/0xB4631), the system object 0xAF1F0 (0xAF6F1) [review 32]'),
    (0x5520A8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "the loading screen''s progress counter: incremented by texture/lightmap/sky loads (0x48B92, 0x52F0E, 0x57F41/0x57F7A, 0x726BA) and the UI (0xAF756, 0xE8C82) when the loading screen 0x5520B4 is up (0x48B6B, 0x52EEA, 0x57F17) [review 32]"),
    (0x5520B4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the loading screen / UI-dialog active flag: written by the Xbox UI (0xBF0E0 at 0xBF0FF, 0xE92C0.., 0xE9660 at 0xE9624), read by the loaders above and the UI [review 32]'),
    (0x5520C4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'a third model-name pointer of 0xC37E0 (0xC3A12), read by the server game (0x16F531): the same map-media selection as 0x5430D8 [review 32]'),
    (0x5522E8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'an XACT / file cache size: 0xC5F40 "Cache" stores 0x33B0, the XACT read callbacks 0x1065B0 / 0x106630 store 0x3434. Sound [review 32]'),
    (0x55230D, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'an Xbox UI flag: UI start-up handlers 0xE4980 / 0xE8610, UI commands 0xD7260 / 0xE6160, the UI frame 0xCD7D0 (called by SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10) [review 32]'),
    (0x55234C, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'the buy-menu-open flag of the Xbox UI (0xCA3D0 at 0xCA3F8.., 0xCA830, scoreboard 0x1BA710, 0x1D4DE0, and the server game rules 0x1462B0). One UI in M2; would need review when each player gets its own menus [review 32]'),
    (0x552364, 0x10, 'shared-mutable', 'Xbox UI timing: 0x552364..0x552370 initialised by 0xC9AB0 (start-up), updated by 0xC9B80 (from the UI frame 0xCD7D0) and 0xC9B30 / 0xE1BF0 (video playback commands) [review 32]'),
    (0x552378, 0x2, 'shared-mutable', 'a word of the Xbox UI (0xCFB20, 0xCFB90 from 0xCD370; taken by the profile UI 0xD8BD0 / 0xD8D50) [review 32]'),
    (0x5523C0, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', "the Xbox UI''s current and previous pad buttons: 0x19E160 copies 0x5523C0 to 0x5523C4 and the pad mask 0x5439B8 to 0x5523C0 (0x19E1CD..0x19E1E1), only while the UI object 0x5523D4 is up; read by the UI (0xCB202, 0xCABD1, 0xCD689). Pad input, only player 1 in M2 [review 32]"),
    (0x5523F9, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'system link / UI: the UI frame 0xCD7D0 and the XNet code 0xED9D0 / 0xEE820 [review 32]'),
    (0x552408, 0x23, 'shared-mutable', "a pending xbui command string for the training tutorial: copied by the server game''s round code (0x144E20 -> 0xE4D90 rep movsd 7 + movsb, 0xE4E30 8 dwords + movsw + movsb = 0x23 bytes, 0xE4ED0, 0xE4F90), consumed and cleared by the UI frame 0xCD7D0 (0xCD831..0xCD85C) [review 32]"),
    (0x5524A0, 0x2, 'shared-mutable', "the Xbox stats subsystem 0xFC710 (objects 0x5590A8, 0x5616D0): the client''s StatsRoundEnd / StatsRoundWin handlers set a flag (0x1A613E, 0x1A61D3) and call into the stats code, which reads and clears both (0xFC7ED, 0xFC80C, 0xFC812; 0xFC6A3). Profile statistics of the console, not client-instance state [review 32]"),
    (0x5526F0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'voice subsystem: 0x102250 (voice init, voice_micdata.wav etc.), 0x102350, 0x1029F0; part of the voice state 0x5526E8..0x552718 shared with 0x101EB0 / 0x101FD0 / 0x102440. Sound, one copy [review 32]'),
    (0x55270C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the same voice subsystem (0x102350 at 0x102365, read by 0x102440 at 0x1024A0; taken by 0x102250 at 0x102290) [review 32]'),
    (0x552AC9, 0x1, 'server', "written by the server game rules (0x143CB0 at 0x143E1F, 0x144E20 at 0x1455E1/0x1456C6/0x145D68, 0x1462B0, 0x147620 at 0x147F45/0x148046) and read by them (0x144D97); the client''s RoundWin handler 0x1A61B0 stores the winner byte from the message (0x1A623E), the value the server just sent. Server-owned, shared [review 32]"),
    (0x552B7C, 0x4, 'player', 'gViewPort (VGUI TeamFortressViewport*). Only dword accesses. Written by 1BAE90@1BAF55 (called from 18B7E0, the client VidInit export: it makes a new 0xA84-byte object at 1BAF10 only if [0x552B7C] is null at 1BAEF1, otherwise it resets the existing one through 1B09A0) and by the constructor 1B03B0@1B03FA. Read by the per-player HUD message forwarders 1A62F0..1A6580 (e.g. 1A62F0 mov ecx,[0x552B7C]), the spectator code 1A8F5E and the HUD. g_VoiceStatus Init receives &gViewPort (1A6B3E push 0x552B7C). Each client’s own messages (VGUI menu, team select, scoreboard) go through it, so it is per-player. RISK: if it is swapped, the added player makes a second viewport parented to the one VGUI root panel (1BAF5F call [edx+0x40] with the root from [0x54321C]). Check that player 1’s VGUI paint does not draw it. [review 64]'),
    (0x552B94, 0x4, 'process', 'client gpGlobals pointer. Its only writer is 18E160@18E17A mov dword ptr [0x552B94],0x5692E0, inside HUD_InitClientWeapons, which is guarded by the once-flag [0x5BDA60] (18E160 test, jnz out; 18E170 sets it to 1, and nothing ever clears it). The pointer is constant once set. The pointee 0x5692E0 (gpGlobals->time, written each call by 18E449 fstp [eax]) is a separate object that must be reviewed on its own. 0x5BDA60 is also process (one writer, 18E170). [review 64]'),
    (0x552B9D, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'write-only byte. Its writers are 31030@31047 (=0) and 18D720@18D725 (=1). There is no read of 0x552B9D anywhere (grep of all forms), and the neighbouring byte 0x552B9C is only read as a byte (1C2978, 1CEF68, 1CF3D7). So ownership does not change behaviour; shared is enough. [review 64]'),
    (0x552BA8, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'per-call prediction flag (bit 3 of [esi+0x290] of the from-state). It is rewritten at every HUD_WeaponsPostThink 18E430@18ED4E (mov cl,bl; shr cl,3; and cl,1) before the shared weapon code reads it (byte reads 11C532, 124839, 13C035, 1394D0...). Nothing carries across calls, and each local player’s prediction runs inside its own turn. The server-role readers are the weapon code shared with the server; they already read the last predicted value in the original game. [review 64]'),
    (0x552C34, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'pm_shared global "pmove" (one playermove_t* shared by engine, client and server code). Every movement entry point sets it to a constant right before running PM code: client side 0x78A6E0 (25BF0@25C28, 25EC0@25EE2, 32EB0@32ED7 just before call 25EC0), server side 0x6524E0 (5E0A0@5E14D, ABEC0, 79FB0). HUD_PlayerMoveInit 18B6C0@18B6CD and 1A5B20@1A5B2F store the argument the engine passes. The value is always one of two fixed addresses, so it can be shared. The pointee g_clmove 0x78A6E0 must be per-player and is reviewed separately. [review 64]'),
    (0x552C68, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'g_runfuncs. HUD_PostRunCmd 18F330@18F350 writes it from its argument at entry, before any read. Its readers (18E430@18EE83/18F014, 18F360, 18E020, 18D840, 1A74B0) all run inside that call (1A74B0 is an engine-func override installed by 18E160@18E1E9). This is call-scoped scratch. [review 64]'),
    (0x552C6C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'player pointer for the call. It is set at 18E430@18EE1D (mov [0x552C6C],ebp) and cleared at the exit, 18E430@18F2A4 (=0). Its only other reader is the callback 1A74B0@1A74C0, which runs inside the call. Scoped scratch. [review 64]'),
    (0x552C78, 0x4, 'player', 'g_weaponselect (input). The HUD weapon-menu code sets it to the chosen weapon id: 1AC320 family@1AC303 mov [0x552C78],ecx with ecx=[esi+0xA0] (hud_cyclerestart, wpn_hudon.wav), the 1AB1D0.. slot handlers, and 1ACC70@1ACCBE (=0). CL_CreateMove-side 190150 reads it at 19031D, copies it into usercmd+0x21 (weaponselect) at 19032F, and clears it at 190332 (esi=0). Its sibling g_impulse 0x552BAC does the same into usercmd+0x20 (190317/190326/190329). Per-player input. 0x552C7C (=1.0f at 1AC309) is a separate field and is not classified here. [review 64]'),
    (0x552C98, 0x4, 'process', 'pointer to the stats object, created once: HUD_Init 1A65A0 reads it at 1A66EA and calls 1B5B80 to make it only if it is null (1A66F5/1A66F7), storing it at 1A66FE. It is read by the stats message handlers 1A5FC0/1A60D0/1A6130 ("STATS: ROUND END")/1A6180 and by the server-side stats 1B6490 (callers E6480/FB300). It belongs to the shared stats subsystem of [67]. If it were swapped, the added player would make a second object that the server never sees. [review 64]'),
    (0x5539F8, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'byte 0 of a renderer-side object at 0x5539F8 that is passed by pointer to C06D0/C1FA0/C0D00/C0870. C21D0@C21D7 sets it to 1 and C2210@C2210 sets it to 0, then jumps to C0870. The only caller of both is SCR_UpdateScreen 55E10, which the added player skips. 6F080@6F208 (a draw-side function called from 1ACB50/C2AC0/CC1C0) also writes it. The rest of the object’s size is not proven; only the byte flag (byte accesses) is classified here. [review 64]'),
    (0x561690, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'stats-session-active flag of the one stats subsystem. Writers: server FC710@FC7A3 (=1), game-rules init F07D0@F0B03 (=0; the function names mp_track_stats), round logic 147620@1476DA, FC6C2@FC700, and the client MsgFunc_ReportStats 1A6260@1A62D3, which only mirrors the server broadcast and starts FC690 on a rising edge (1A62C2..1A62DC). One flag for the console. [review 64]'),
    (0x56169C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'stats state id. FC870@FC94E stores the argument ebx (compared with 0x270F at FC8CC). FC870 is called from both the HUD init 1A65A0 and the server 144D30/1A6130/1B5DA0; it is read by FC690@FC69A and FC710@FC767/FC7E4 (server). Same subsystem as 0x561690. If per-user Live stats are ever needed per local player, this decision has to be revisited. [review 64]'),
    (0x5619E4, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'Xbox UI/shell state. Its writers all store 0: E9660@E963D ("xbui open HighLatency"), E9420@E945D ("NetworkNotFound"), E9480@E94BD ("LiveConnectionLost"). Neighbouring bytes 5619E5..E7 are xbui flags as well (F6DE0 is hub). Shell, shared. [review 64]'),
    (0x56D684, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'scratch vec3. It is written by three dword stores, 18E430@18EC95, 18EC9E and 18ECA7 (from [0x3A0AC4]+8 offsets 0/4/8), and its address is passed at 18ECFE push 0x56D684 to [0x543238]+0x3C at 18ED03. There is no other reader (who 56D660..56D6A0). Fully rewritten before each use. 0x56D66C..0x56D683 (18ECB0..18ECE1) is the same kind of scratch. 0x56D690..0x56D69F is a different object (console and spectator writers); it was not reviewed here. [review 64]'),
    (0x57F0A8, 0x3E800, 'player', 'grid of 40*40*40 dword pointers. Extent comes from the clear loop in 1CC5D0: 1CC63D edi=0x57F0A8, inner ecx=0x28 with stride 0xA0 (1CC652/1CC666), middle esi=0x28 with stride 4 (1CC644/1CC66E), outer edi+=0x1900 with bound cmp edi,0x5BD8A8 (1CC674/1CC67A). The same loop at 1CC6B4..1CC6FA and the boot constructor 23F270 confirm it. Index at 1DE6B0: (arg*40 + y/10)*40 + x/10 (1DEA52..1DEA8A), then mov [ecx*4+0x57F0A8],esi at 1DEA9E. Cleared by 1CC5D0, called from the client init 18B970/1A5EE0. Filled by 1DE6B0 (client effect creation, strings militia/sprites/glass_01.spr), read via 1DE74C and 1DECCB. It holds pointers to that client’s own effect objects, so it is per-player. Those objects must be per-player too. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BD8C4, 0x18, 'shared-mutable', 'CMiniMem allocator state (strings at 1F8E40: "CMiniMem Free", "Particles Drawn"). 0x5BD8C4 is a list head (1F9D16..1F9D40, 1FA51F..1FA542). 0x5BD8C8 is a vector object: begin 5BD8CC, end 5BD8D0, cap 5BD8D4 (1F9C5E push 0x5BD8C8; 1FA500..1FA515 size=(end-begin)>>2; atexit 240160 clears all three). 0x5BD8D8 is the second list head (1F9DE0, 1F9E40). All of 5BD8C4..5BD8DB must have one owner, because the lists thread through heap blocks owned by the vector; never split them. It is an allocator for visual particles drawn by 1F8E40, so it is classified shared. NOTE: if shared, particles spawned by the added player’s event playback land in player 1’s view. Making it per-player would need the heap blocks (5BD8C8 vector) and 5BD8B0/5BD8B4/5BD8E0 per-player too. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BDA10, 0x10, 'process', '113AB0: guard bit 0 of [0x5C9638] (113AB1 test; 113AC3 or). Then four dword stores 113AC9..113ADB (-1,-1,-1,1). Its address is returned when the index is -1 (113AF3). Set once ever. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BDA24, 0x10, 'process', '115610: guard [0x5C9634] (115611/115623), four dword stores 115629..11563B, returned at 115656. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BDA34, 0x8, 'process', '115EC0: guard [0x5C9630] (115EC1/115ED5), four word stores 115EDB..115EF0, returned at 115F10. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BDBD0, 0x2C, 'player', 'client_textmessage_t (effect, r1..a1, r2..a2, x, y, fadein, fadeout, holdtime, fxtime, pName, pMessage), fully written by 1B3F50 at 1B3F69..1B3FF0 (the last field is 1B3FE6 [0x5BDBF8]=0x5BDC00 and pName 1B3FF0). It is then handed to the HUD message code 1D35B0 with edx=0x56375C (inside gHUD), which keeps the pointer for drawing. Called from the per-player HUD code 18B970/1DA6F0. gHUD is per-player, so this message it references must be per-player too. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BDC00, 0x80, 'player', 'its text buffer: 1B3F50 push 0x80 / push eax / push 0x5BDC00 / call 22CA40 (strncpy with count 0x80) at 1B3F50..1B3F5B. pMessage points here. [review 64]'),
    (0x5BEFB8, 0x800, 'shared-mutable', 'parsemsg READ_STRING (1D5E10) static char[2048]. Copy loop bound: inc ecx; cmp ecx,0x7FF; jb at 1D5E57..1D5E5E, then the terminator mov [ecx+0x5BEFB8],bl at 1D5E63, so the maximum index is 0x7FF. Rewritten at every call and the pointer is returned at 1D5E69. The callers checked consume it at once (pushed to copy/print calls: 1A64E1, 1B5575, 1B55A6, 1D5F15, 1D7F59). Not every caller was checked for keeping the pointer (e.g. 1B591E and 1D776D keep it in a register for a while). If any caller keeps it across turns, it must become player. [review 64]'),
    (0x5C9630, 0xC, 'process', 'the three guard dwords 5C9630/5C9634/5C9638. Only writers are the or-at-first-call above. [review 64]'),
    (0x5C9640, 0x4, 'process', 'FC870: guard bit 0 of [0x5C9660] (FC870 test al,1; FC88D or). Inside the guard: QueryPerformanceFrequency-like 200E3D, then fild/fdivr, then fstp [0x5C9640] at FC8C6 (1/frequency). Never written again. The other fields 5C9648..5C9658 are rewritten later (FC920..FC944) and are not part of this entry. [review 64]'),
    (0x5CBB70, 0x4, 'process', 'guard for the static 0x40x0x7C array at 0x5C9C70 (1BB207 or [0x5CBB70],1; 1BB20E..1BB22C: eh-vector-ctor 22DDBD(0x5C9C70, 0x7C, 0x40, ctor 1BB030, dtor 1BB050), atexit 240120). It is inside the viewport scheme loader 1BB190, which the viewport ctor 1B03B0 calls. The guard’s owner must match the array’s owner. If 0x5C9C70 were ever made per-player, this guard must be too. [review 64]'),
    (0x5CBBC8, 0x4, 'process', 'guard for the static object 0x5CBBA8 built by C8230 (19E160@19E2D8 or; 19E2DE esi=0x5CBBA8). Same dependency on the guarded object. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D0E90, 0x4, 'process', 'Xbox UI option-list static guard (CF1A0@CF1C7; object around 0x5D0E20 built at CF1E4..CF207; strings Right-Handed/Left-Handed). Constant UI labels. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D0ECC, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CF0A0@CF0C2 (Appear Offline/Online). [review 64]'),
    (0x5D0EEC, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CEF90@CEFCB. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D0F28, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CEE90@CEEB2 (Standard/Random). [review 64]'),
    (0x5D1048, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CEAE0@CEB07. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D10DC, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CE930@CE957 (Very Low..Very High). [review 64]'),
    (0x5D1134, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CE7A0@CE7C2 (Off/Auto). [review 64]'),
    (0x5D1170, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CE6A0@CE6C2. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D1494, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CEDB0@CEDD5. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D14C0, 0x4, 'process', 'same pattern, CF310@CF37B. CF310 is the options-menu builder that calls all of the above. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D350C, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'local static in CCD20 (recursive UI layout via CD030/CD230; static init through DA540 at CCDB6 push 0x5D350C). It is fully rewritten on both paths before it is read: 5D350C,5D3510,5D3514,5D3518,5D351C at CCDF3..CCE22 or CCE7C..CCEAB, and read from CCE44/CCF09 onward. Scratch, Xbox UI. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D3520, 0x4, 'process', 'its init guard: CCDAB or [0x5D3520],eax; cleared only by the EH funclet 23C400. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D8EBC, 0x4, 'player', 'hud_spectator global iJumpSpectator. Set to 1 by the spectator target functions 1A9000@1A9192 ("follownext"), 1A91B0, 1A9330, 1A9480 and 1A8740 (map camera points). Set from the DirectorMessage path 18B970@1A8E02. Reset by CHudSpectator Init 1A82C0@1A8353 / 1AA9F0@1AAA2F. Read and cleared by the view code 1A3740@1A3762/1A37B7 (client DLL view; its "server" role comes from reachability through 1A5490). Per-client spectator state with dword accesses only. The neighbours vJumpOrigin/vJumpAngles should follow it. [review 64]'),
    (0x5D8F40, 0x4800, 'shared-mutable', 'sound subsystem: 16 slots of 0x480 bytes. Extent: Host_Init 5D9E0 clears it with edx=0x5D8F40 (5DCF6) and ecx=0x1200 dwords, rep stosd (5DCFF/5DD04). Slot formula in 1018B0: lea edx,[eax+eax*8]; shl edx,7 (=eax*0x480) at 1018D4/1018D7, with eax<0x10 from 101850 (cmp eax,0x10 at 1018A3; scan bound cmp ecx,0x5DDBE0). The caller 100F10 is S_StartDynamicSound. The sound path is shared, and the added player starts no sound in M2. [review 64]'),
    (0x5E13A0, 0x38, 'player', 'per-connection auth handshake state of the local client. Extent: B6E40 (startup) stores 14 dwords 5E13A0..5E13D4 (B6E5D..B6EA5) and does rep stosd over the same 0x38 (B6EBA/B6EBF). Players write it in CL_ConnectionlessPacket 27CE0 (calls B6D00 "Server challenge/auth" and B7220 "constructing authentication request"; ebx=0x5E13A0 at 28065/2811F) and in CL_CheckForResend 5D2E0 through B70D0 (retry counter 5E13C0, timer 5E13B8). Each local client connects on its own (M2), so it is per-player. [review 64]'),
    (0x5E32E0, 0x34, 'player', 'V_ScreenShake state (amplitude, frequency, duration, next-shake time, offsets). Extent: B6770 does 13 dword clears 5E32E0..5E3310 (B677B..B67C3) and rep stosd over 52 bytes (B67D3/B67D8), called from the map/world init 4F8D0. Written by the user-message handler B6460, registered at 1C67F push 0xB6460 inside client message-hook setup 1C5D0 (strings ScreenShake/ScreenFade). Each player receives its own ScreenShake messages. Consumed by B6200/B63F0 (view calc/apply, render side). Per-player so the added player’s shakes do not move player 1’s view. [review 64]'),
    (0x5E4320, 0x10, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer state: four floats. Cleared by V_UpdatePalette B5A00@B5A11..B5A2F (only caller SCR_UpdateScreen 55E10) and by 4DC00@4DF4D..4DF6B (gl=5, render). Blended by 4B5B0 (caller 4B620, gl=6). Only player 1 draws. [review 64]'),
    (0x5E6460, 0x800, 'player', 'text buffer for the HUD text-message channels. In 38310 (parse TE_TEXTMESSAGE, caller 30D90): channel = byte & 0x80000003 with sign fix (38349..38355), so 0..3; message parms entry = 0x37A050 + ch*0x2C (3835A/38360); buffer = ch<<9 + 0x5E6460 (38637/3863A); copy at most 0x1FF (38646), then terminator mov byte ptr [ebp+0x5E665F],0 at 3866F. So the extent is 4*0x200. The parms ([esi+0x28]=buffer at 38643) are handed to the client HUD via "HudText" (3868B/38690), and the HUD keeps them to draw. Received in each player’s packet parse. The parms array 0x37A050..0x37A100 (4*0x2C) belongs with it and should also be player. [review 64]'),
    (0x5EF7A0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'engine host state giActive (DLL_PAUSED 2, CLOSE 3, TRANS 4, RESTART 5): 5E7A0@5E7A0 (=5, restart command), 63290@632A3 (=4, changelevel2), quit paths 21F90@2212C/22143 and 5E740@5E756 (=3), Host_Error AC090@AC16F (=2), each paired with giStateInfo 0x551F98=4. Startup 5D9E0@5DD81. It drives the one main loop, so it is process-wide. [review 64]'),
    (0x5EF7C0, 0x46418, 'server', 'server_t sv. Extent: 5CC60 sets eax=0x5EF7C0, then edi=eax, ecx=0x11906, rep stosd (5CCD9..5CCE7), 0x11906*4=0x46418. Written by the server (78E70, 7B1C0, 961C0, SV_SpawnServer 9FEF0...). The "player" writes are Host_ShutdownServer 5C9D0@[0x5EF7C0] (sv.active=0) and the clear 5CC60, called from the client disconnect path 28E60. NOTE: an added player’s disconnect running 5C9D0 or 5CC60 would shut down the one server; that path must be blocked for non-primary players. [review 64]'),
    (0x636D14, 0x4, 'server', 'server logging file handle. Log_Open 942E0@944DC, Log_Close 942A0@942C8 ("Log file closed"), and Host_ShutdownServer 5C9D0@5CBA4 / Host_Shutdown 5DDA0@5DFFD close it. Read by Log_Printf 94090@9415D and SV_SpawnServer 9FEF0@9FF81. Server-owned and shared. [review 64]'),
    (0x638198, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'every store writes 0: 30960@309A3 (=0), and SV_SpawnServer 9FEF0@A00ED/A0655 store ebx, which is 0 from 9FF10 xor ebx,ebx and is not reassigned on that path (the only pop ebx, A047C, is an early-return). No address-taken uses. Read by render (4DDE6, 4ECB2, 4ED19), client (33605) and server (6BD95, 6BFD4). After the first clear it is 0 for the process, so swapping it would not change anything. Identity not established. [review 64]'),
    (0x63B000, 0x4, 'server', 'server globalvars_t time, set by the server frame (A3BB0, A3C40, A50A0, A6470 fstp; A9210 mov) and SV_SpawnServer/changelevel (9FEC0, 63290, 7B930, 97B60). Address passed at AC820/ACC17 push 0x63B000. The "player" writer is Host_ShutdownServer 5C9D0. Server-owned. Only this 4-byte field is classified. [review 64]'),
    (0x69DFA0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: written to 1.0f by R_DrawSpriteModel 4C570@4C61E (gl=20), by 4D0D0@4D23E and by glow 93600@9395E (gl=7). Read throughout the entity draw (4EC60 R_DrawEntitiesOnList, 50ED0, 51780). GL/render state; only player 1 draws. [review 64]'),
    (0x6A8198, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'r_part state: active_particles 6A8198, a second active list 6A819C, num_particles 6A81A0, particle pool pointer 6A81A4, free_particles 6A81A8. R_InitParticles 82EB0 (startup) sets the count (82ED7/82EEA: -particles, min 0x200, default 0x800) and allocates one heap pool of count*0x38+0x10 (82EEF..82EF8). R_ClearParticles 830F0 resets the lists over that pool (83103..8310F, 83120 loop with stride 0x38). The allocators 833D0, 83EB0, 83170 and 24A90 unlink from the free list. All five fields thread through the one heap pool, so they must share one owner with the pool. Shared like a renderer subsystem. NOTE: the added player’s tempent parse (833D0 via 30D70) then adds particles to player 1’s view. Per-player particles would need a separate pool, not just swapped heads. [review 64]'),
    (0x6A81C0, 0x100, 'shared-mutable', 'cl_beamentities[64] with count 0x6A84C4: every append checks cmp count,0x40 / jnl (1C910@1CA1C, 1D41D@1D46C, 24EF0@24FC5), then mov [count*4+0x6A81C0],ptr. The count is reset every frame by CL_EmitEntities 264E0@264F1 (ebp=0 from 264E6) before the appends, and the list is consumed by the beam drawing 871D0/89C60 in the same turn. Per-frame scratch. The pointed-to cl_entity_t must be valid in the turn that draws. 0x6A84C4 (4 bytes) goes with it as shared-mutable. [review 64]'),
    (0x6A82C0, 0x204, 'shared-mutable', 'R_BeamDraw 0x896E0 writes [0]=0 at 89730 and [128]=0 at 89740 (0x6A84C0), then either fills 0x6A82C0..0x6A84C0 with the sin loop 89761..8977B (cmp eax, 0x6A84C0 at 8976B) or calls the fractal 0x87CB0(0x6A82C0, 0x80) at 89781..8978B. So 129 floats, rewritten at the start of every beam draw. Read only by the beam segment code 87EA0@8820D, 884B0@885CC, 88F70@89263, all called from 896E0, which is reached from 871D0/89C60 <- 865D0 <- R_RenderView 0x4EC60 (drawing only). Renderer scratch. [review 96]'),
    (0x6A84C4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the count of the list 0x6A81C0[64]. CreateVisibleEntity 0x1D41D for type 3 checks cmp ecx, 0x40 at 1D46C, stores [ecx*4+0x6A81C0] at 1D475 and the count at 1D482. Same at 1CA17..1CA29 and 24FC0..24FD2. CL_EmitEntities resets it to 0 at 264F1 at the start of every client half. Read only by 1C910, 1D41D and 24EF0 (the appenders) and by the beam drawing 871D0@871D6/87368 and 89C60@89C6A (reached only from R_RenderView 0x4EC60). The list is rebuilt before every use in the same turn. 1D41D is the engine function the client DLL calls from HUD_CreateEntities, [0x7D6CF4] at 26591, inside 264E0. src/game/client_context_regions.inc currently swaps 0x6A81C0+0x100 and 0x6A84C4+4. That is harmless (correct either way), but not needed. [review 96]'),
    (0x6A9500, 0x84, 'server', "SV_SetMoveVars 0x96C30 writes every field 0x6A9500..0x6A9580 from the server cvars (96C49..96D51, 0x6A9528 = 1.0 at 96CD1). It copies skyName[32] at 0x6A9544 with a 0x1F limit (96D5C, base 0x6A9544 at 96D61) and the terminator at 0x6A9563 (96D8D). 17 dwords + 32 chars + 8 dwords = 0x84. Its callers 96DA0/97060/9FEF0 are server code. The client writer is CL_ParseMovevars (svc_newmovevars; the function the tool calls 0x31130, instructions 2F530..), which copies the same values from net_message (0x6BA588 / msg_readcount 0x748404). Every local client gets them from the same built-in server, so they are identical. The server's own player movement uses the shared copy. One copy, owned by the server. [review 96]"),
    (0x6BA590, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the cursize field of the sizebuf net_message 0x6BA580 (flags 0x6BA584, data 0x6BA588, cursize 0x6BA590; analysis/netcode_engine.md). Every packet read sets it (server 69540/6955D/6A2C0/6AD10/6AD60; the client demo readers 22449/22940). The network layer, rewritten before each use. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CA620, 0x100, 'shared-mutable', '0x6B1B0 (the netchan progress update, called from CL_ReadPackets 0x28A40 and 0x2AC80) clears [0] at 6B1E5 and the percent 0x3776DC at 6B1DB on every call. It then copies the fragment file name into it with a 0xFF limit (mov esi, 0xFF at 6B2C1, base 0x6CA620 at 6B2B8) and the terminator at 0x6CA71F (6B2E7): 256 bytes. No absolute reader exists in the code (who.py 6CA620..6CA720: only these writes). It is display state, rewritten on every call. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CDFEC, 0x4, 'server', 'the server global host_client (analysis/netcode_engine.md: SV_SendClientMessages 0x9E413). Written by the server loops (96330, 994D0, 9C680, ...), the host commands and Host_ShutdownServer 0x5C9D0 (which walks the server clients to drop them). It points into svs.clients. Not client state. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE100, 0x30, 'shared-mutable', 'R_ClearSkyBox 0x58A40 writes 9999.0 (0x461C3C00) to 12 dwords 0x6CE100..0x6CE12C, two rows of 6 (58A40..58B08). Read and updated by ClipSkyPolygon/DrawSkyPolygon 0x58200 (lea [eax*4+0x6CE100/0x6CE118] at 58385/58390) and read by R_DrawSkyBox 0x58D10 (58DD0..58F04). 58A40 is called from 0x521B0 <- R_RenderView 0x4EC60 on every view. Renderer scratch. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE140, 0x30, 'shared-mutable', 'same function, -9999.0 (0xC61C3C00) into 12 dwords 0x6CE140..0x6CE16C (58A5E..58B26; 24 stores in all in 58A40, who.py). Same readers (583B3/583BA, 58DD7..58F0B). [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE1E0, 0x18, 'shared-mutable', 'R_LoadSkys 0x57E50 stores [esi+0x6CE1E0] at 57F0E in a loop esi += 4, cmp esi, 0x18 (57FB9/57FBC), and [ebp*4+0x6CE1E0] at 581A0 with ebp < 6 (58012). 6 GL texture numbers for the map sky (skyName 0x6A9544), loaded from R_NewMap 0x4F8D0. Read by R_DrawSkyBox 58D10@58EA2. One GL context; the same map gives the same values. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE240, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'written only (29F5F, 306C4, 3091E, 5585E, 55CF9, 55D28, 5BD85); who.py finds no reader. Screen/loading state next to the above. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE274, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'GL viewport int (one of the four passed by address to GL_BeginRendering 0x56A10: push 0x6CE274 / mov edx, 0x6CE27C / mov ecx, 0x6CE3C8 / mov esi, 0x6CE528 at 55EC2..55ED6, and in 4F330). Written by video init 0xC6F70 (service), the vid_mode command 0xC7330, R_SetupGL 0x4E030 (4E0A9), and the sub-view code 0xB4560, which sets it for a sub-view (B45F9) and restores it after (B472B). One GL context. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE278, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "scr_disabled_for_loading. Set by SCR_BeginLoadingPlaque 0x55CB0 (55D1E) and Host_EndGame 0x5BC40 (5BC82, cleared 5BCF7). Read and cleared by SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10 (55E43/55E78). State of the one screen. Caveat: an added player's connect and disconnect paths also write it (CL_ParseServerInfo-like 0x29F20 at 29F55 = 0, 0x30910, 0x5BC40). In M2 that can only end or start player 1's loading plaque early (display only). [review 96]"),
    (0x6CE27C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'as 0x6CE274 (B45E0 set, B471F restore; C7330/C6F70). [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE288, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the loading-plaque draw flag. 55CB0 sets 1 (55CEF); 29F20/30910/31A90/5BD30 clear it. Read by SCR_UpdateScreen 55E35 and the view 0xB4560 (B4645/B46C3). Screen state; same caveat as 0x6CE278. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE290, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'written only: 0x65130 (from the view B4560) sets 1 at 6516E, SCR_UpdateScreen clears it at 55E4A. No reader. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE2BC, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'video/console size pair, written by GL_BeginRendering 56A10 (56A49/56A5A), video init C6F70 (C72A5/C72B0), vid_mode C7330 (C746D/C7478) and AF0A0 (AF10B/AF119); two exact dwords. One display. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE2CC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "the recalc-refdef flag. Set by the viewsize commands 55970/559B0 and by client message handlers 30A90/31060/31090/B5960. Cleared by SCR_CalcRefdef 0x55850 (55864). Read by SCR_UpdateScreen 55EDB to call the recalculation. An extra set by another player only recomputes player 1\\'s refdef once more. [review 96]"),
    (0x6CE2D8, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'as 0x6CE2BC (56A43/56A55, C72A0/C72AA, C7468/C7472); no reader found. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE2F0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'scr_disabled_time. Only writer 55CB0 (fstp at 55D15), only reader SCR_UpdateScreen 55E56. Screen state. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE3C8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the third GL_BeginRendering pointer (mov ecx, 0x6CE3C8 at 55EC7, 4F410..). Written by C6F70 (C7295), C7330 (C745D), R_SetupGL 4E0AE, and B4560 (B45ED set, B4725 restore). Renderer/display. [review 96]'),
    (0x6CE528, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the fourth GL_BeginRendering pointer (mov esi, 0x6CE528 at 55ED1, 4F41A). Written by C6F70 (C728F), C7330 (C7457), B4560 (B45D3 set, B4719 restore). Renderer/display. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E63A0, 0x1440, 'shared-mutable', 'R_BuildLightMap 0x4FD80 refuses smax*tmax > 0x144 (cmp esi, 0x144 at 4FE0D, Sys_Error 4FE35). It initialises exactly smax*tmax samples of 0x10 bytes (r,g,b dwords at 0x6E63A0/A4/A8) before use: the fill loop 4FE9F..4FEB0 or the clear 4FEEE..4FF18 (add eax, 0x10). Then it accumulates the light styles (4FF5B..4FF88). R_AddDynamicLights 0x4FB10 adds the dlights ([ecx+0x6E63A0..A8]). 0x144*0x10 = 0x1440, ending at 0x6E77E0. Renderer scratch, rewritten for the used extent before each use. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7800, 0x200, 'shared-mutable', 'R_BlendLightmaps 0x51000 walks esi = 0..0x7F (inc esi; cmp esi, 0x80 at 51315/51316): it reads [esi*4+0x6E7800] at 51176 and clears it at 511B7 after drawing. Surfaces set entry [surf+0x38] (the lightmap texture number) during the world draw: 50420@505EB, 513C0@51513. GL_BuildLightmaps 0x529C0 (R_NewMap) sets [ebp*4] at 52C6A. 128 dwords, ending at 0x6E7A00 (where the function pointer 0x6E7A00 begins). Renderer state of the shared GL lightmap pages. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7A20, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "r_refdef (docs/native_splitscreen.md: renderer per-view scratch, kept shared). Written by SCR_CalcRefdef 0x55850, V_RenderView\\'s setup 0xB5D10 and the envmap command 0x4F330. All are drawing or console paths; an added player never draws in M2. [review 96]"),
    (0x6E7A90, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'r_refdef.vieworg, set per view by 0xB5D10 (B5D12/B5D1B/B5D24) and adjusted by V_RenderView 0xB5E90 (B60C6..B616E) and 0x1DC00 (1DD2F..1DD3B; called only from B5E90). Read by R_SetupFrame 0x4DC00, R_SetupGL 0x4E030 and the world draw: drawing only. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7A9C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'r_refdef.viewangles[0]; set by B5D10 (B5D2D), 1DC00 (1DD4A) and the envmap command 4F330. Read by renderer functions (4DC00, 4E030). Per-view scratch. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7AD0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'a counter updated read-modify-write only by renderer code: R_RenderView 0x4EF00 (sets 4EF6A), 4CBD0 (4CF08/4CF13), R_SetupFrame 4DF47, the studio/world model renderer 194E80/196240, and 91FB0 (gl=9). All reached from the draw. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7BA0, 0x400, 'shared-mutable', "R_NewMap 0x4F8D0 sets all 256 entries to 0x108 (loop cmp [ebp-4], 0x100 at 4F8E7, store 4F8F3). R_AnimateLight 0x4B550 (from R_SetupFrame 0x4DC00 <- R_RenderView) recomputes entries 0..63 (cmp ecx, 0x6E7CA0 at 4B59D) from cl_lightstyle (0x7863E0, stride 0x44) and cl.time (0x74A290) on every view. Indexed by a byte (movzx edx, dl; [edx*4+0x6E7BA0] at 4FF4D/4FF50). Renderer table, rebuilt in the drawing player\\'s view. Readers outside the draw (R_LightPoint 0x4BA90 via 0x4BE50 <- 0x8FDA0/0x90013) see the last drawn view\\'s values, as in the title. [review 96]"),
    (0x6E7FA8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'R_RenderView 4EF00 sets 0 (4EF79), 51630 sets 1 (51706). Read by R_SetupGL 4E26C, 51F40 and R_MarkLeaves 0x52380 (523BD). Renderer flag. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7FB0, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'a 3-float renderer colour/vector, written by the entity draw 0x4CBD0 (4CE3D..4CEB6, normalised in place) and set to constants by the GL-heavy callbacks 0x90DD0 (gl=20; 90DED..90E01) and 0x92C30 (92C49..92C5D). Three exact dwords. Drawing scratch. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E7FD0, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', "r_origin. Written only by R_SetupFrame 0x4DC00 (4DE4C/4DE52/4DE57), read by the renderer (4B620, 4C570, 4CBD0, 58970, 58B40, 3AF80 <- 871D0/93000/93600) and the console (5E880/5ED30); 1C2A0/1C350 take its address. In M2 only player 1\\'s draw writes it. [review 96]"),
    (0x6E7FEC, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'r_viewleaf (0x6E7FEC) and r_oldviewleaf (0x6E7FF0). R_SetupFrame 4DC00: old = view (4DE62/4DE76), then view = new leaf (4DE81). R_MarkLeaves 0x52380 compares them (5238F/5239C) and updates the old one (523E7). R_NewMap 4F95C clears the view leaf. CL_EmitEntities forces a re-mark (265A9 = 0; call 52380 at 265AF); the server map code 77B10/77B8D does too. The leaf marks they gate live in the one shared world model, so these must stay one copy with them. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E8770, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'written by the entity draw code only: 4CBD0 (4CC79), R_DrawEntitiesOnList 0x4D0D0 (4D2A2/4D2C1), the sprite draw 0x93600 (93739/93753; "Non-sprite set to glow!"). Read by 4C570, 4CBD0 and 931F0 (<- 93600). All are reached from R_RenderView 0x4EC60. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E88BC, 0x4, 'player', 'the sibling mask, written by the same code (2A80F reset, 2A5EA/2A634/2A694, 254B0@24D4B) from the per-player cl_dlights. No reader besides these read-modify-writes (who.py), so sharing would also be harmless. It follows 0x6E88C0. [review 96]'),
    (0x6E88C0, 0x4, 'player', "the active-dlight mask read by R_BuildLightMap 4FD80@4FDE7 in the draw. CL_DecayLights 0x2A7F0 rebuilds it from cl_dlights (2A815 = 0, 2A8B4 store). That runs at 5D540, after SCR_UpdateScreen (5D52D), at the end of each player\\'s client half. CL_AllocDlight 0x2A510 (the client\\'s efx entry, used inside the turn) ORs bits in (2A5F0, 2A63C, 2A69F) during the next frame. The value player 1 draws with is carried over from its previous turn. If shared, player 2\\'s CL_DecayLights would replace it with player 2\\'s lights. [review 96]"),
    (0x723268, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'incremented and wrapped at 1500 texture names (inc ecx; cmp ecx, 0x5DC at 72871/72873, store 72879; the same pattern in the sky loader 57EEF/57EF5). Used by GL_LoadTexture 0x48880 ("Texture Overflow: MAX_GLTEXTURES"; 488C2/488D3/489A6), 491F0, C9D10, 529C0, 140CE. It hands out GL texture names in the one GL context. A per-player copy would make two players allocate the same names. Must be one copy. [review 96]'),
    (0x742FC0, 0x1000, 'shared-mutable', "Draw_DecalSetName 0x430C0 bounds the index with cmp eax, 0x100 (430C0), scales it by 16 (shl eax, 4 at 430CA) and copies at most 15 chars (mov esi, 0x0F at 430D2) plus the terminator [edi+0x742FCF] (430FD). Cleared at start-up by 0x46E30 (rep stosd, ecx = 0x400 dwords at 46EE2/46EE7). Read by Draw_DecalTexture 0x43110 (shl ecx, 4; lea [ecx+0x742FC0]) and 0x43310. Filled from the server\\'s decal list (0x282E0/0x30F60): the same index-to-name map for every local client of the one server, tied to the process\\'s decal textures. [review 96]"),
    (0x7492A0, 0x1C, 'shared-mutable', '7 dwords. Initialised per map by 0x33A50 (33A6E..33A92 = 0, then 33A9C..33ABA; called from 0x2D350) and by its loader 0x33620 (33971..33A3A). Changed and read by the overview draw 0x33C10 (from R_RenderView 4EC60), read by R_SetupGL 4E030 (4E1BE..4E205). A renderer display setting from the map, the same for every client on the map; only the drawing player changes it. [review 96]'),
    (0x7492E0, 0x100, 'player', "the per-svc message counts[64]. CL_ParseServerMessage 0x30260 bounds them with cmp esi, 0x3F at 3043A and increments inc [esi*4+0x7492E0] at 30443. Cleared by Q_memset(0x7492E0, 0, 0x100) in the connect paths 27B2B..27B37 and 29DA7..29DB3. Written by each client\\'s own parse and reset by its own connect. Read only by the cl_messages stats command 0x2FEA0 (2FEC0). Debug statistics; sharing would mix the players\\' counts. [review 96]"),
    (0x749400, 0x708, 'process', "CL_ParseStartSoundPacket (0x2F160; the tool names 0x30E50, which is jmp 0x2F160) queues a sound only while [0x5518A4] == 0 (2F36E/2F375) and the count 0x5518B0 < 0x32 (2F37D). Entry address = count*0x24 (lea eax, [ecx+ecx*8]; shl eax, 2 at 2F386/2F389), 9 dwords at 0x749400..0x749420 (2F38C..2F3D4). 50*0x24 = 0x708. The queue is replayed once by 0x2F420 (esi from 0x749404, add esi, 0x24 at 2F4DB) when the start-up routine 0xAD8A0 sets [0x5518A4] = 1 (ADDD5) and calls 0x2F420 (ADDE3). 0x5518A4 has no other writer, so the queue is used only before the process\\'s start-up completes and never again. A player added later never writes it. [review 96]"),
    (0x749B20, 0x100, 'player', '64 dwords accumulated by 0x2FF50 (from CL_ParseServerMessage 0x30260) from the per-packet sizes 0x749C20[64]: loop add eax, 0x10; cmp eax, 0x100 at 2FFA2/2FFA5. Cleared by Q_memset(0x749B20, 0, 0x100) at 27B3C..27B48 and 29DB8..29DC4 in the connect paths. Read only by the stats command 2FEA0@2FEDC. Same reasoning as 0x7492E0. [review 96]'),
    (0x749D20, 0x4, 'player', "the count of cl_visedicts 0x785BC0, kept below 0x200 (cmp ecx, 0x200 at 1D445, 25200, 25536, 4B502). Reset by CL_EmitEntities at 264EB and appended by 1C910 (1CA09), 1D41D (1D45E) and 3AE00 (3AF01), all in the client\\'s own frame. Swapping is always correct. Sharing (what docs/native_splitscreen.md 11.1 assumes) is correct only if every reader runs after the same turn\\'s rebuild. The draw readers do (4D0D0; 26290 inside 264E0). Not proven for 0x12000@1201D/122BF, the pickup-hint visible-entity iterator, called from the client game\\'s 0x1CEF20 at a phase I could not establish statically (no static caller; no pointer to it in .data/.rdata). If 0x1CEF20 is proven to run only after 264E0 in the turn (HUD think/redraw, not CL_CreateMove), shared-mutable is also fine. [review 96]"),
    (0x780DE0, 0x500, 'player', "CL_AllocDlight 0x2A510 scans 32 entries of 0x28 (add eax, 0x28; cmp ecx, 0x20 at 2A52B/2A52E and 2A555/2A558). Each entry\\'s die time [+0x14] is compared with the player\\'s cl.time 0x74A290 (2A543). CL_ClearState 0x28E60 clears 0x140 dwords (28EA6..28EB5) on each connect. Decayed by CL_DecayLights 2A7F0 each frame (base 0x780DEC at 2A81D). The lights persist across frames on the player\\'s own clock; read by the renderer (4FB10@4FB55..4FBB1). 2A510 is the client\\'s efx allocator, called from the client\\'s own frame. [review 96]"),
    (0x785BA0, 0x8, 'player', "0x785BA0 is a heap pointer and 0x785BA4 its size. CL_ProcessFile-path 0x285F0 frees the old buffer (2876B), stores the size from 0x7833D4 (28778) and the new block from 0xC9170 (2878E). CL_ClearState frees it on each connect (28E76..28E8D) and zeroes both (28ED3/28ED9); CL_Init zeroes both (2C1A0/2C1A6). Each player\\'s own heap block: if shared, one player\\'s CL_ClearState would free another\\'s buffer. Two exact dwords. [review 96]"),
    (0x785BC0, 0x800, 'player', 'cl_visedicts[512]: index < 0x200 (1D445) times 4 (mov [ecx*4+0x785BC0] at 1D451; 1CA01; 3AEF9). Same ownership as its count 0x749D20 ([120]); the same caveat about the reader 0x12000@12030. [review 96]'),
    (0x7874E0, 0xA00, 'player', "CL_AllocElight 0x2A6B0 (called from 0x90BE0 and the client\\'s efx table) scans 64 entries of 0x28 (add eax, 0x28; cmp ecx, 0x40 at 2A6CA/2A6CD and 2A6F5/2A6F8). It compares die times with cl.time 0x74A290 (2A6E3). CL_ClearState clears 0x280 dwords (28EB7..28EC3) on each connect. Persistent per player, as cl_dlights. [review 96]"),
    (0x7D6170, 0x4, 'player', "0x22A40 is entry 13 of cl_enginefuncs 0x371610 (pointer at 0x371644), pfnSetCrosshair. It stores the sprite at 22A6B, the rect at 0x7D6180..0x7D618C (22A75..22A92) and r,g,b at 0x7D6164..0x7D616C (22A9E..22AAA). Reset per connect by 0x1CAC0 (from 0x2E780) at 1CAF4. Read by the crosshair draw 0x22AB0 (22AB3; from 0x65130 <- the view 0xB4560). The caller is each player\\'s HUD (the weapon messages). If shared, player 2\\'s HUD would set the crosshair player 1 draws. The sibling fields 0x7D6164+0xC and 0x7D6180+0x10 (exact dword stores above) belong with it. [review 96]"),
    (0x7D67C0, 0xA, 'shared-mutable', 'a 10-byte message-shaped block (word, word, word, 4 bytes) filled field by field just before each call to V_ScreenFade 0xB6500 (1FF43..1FF6C then call at 1FF73; 1FF88..1FFB1; 22759..22785 and 227CE..227FA). B6500 reads exactly [eax], [eax+2], [eax+4], [eax+6..9] (B6504..B6557) into cl.sf (0x74A248.., inside cl). Scratch, fully rewritten before each use. [review 96]'),
    (0x7D67E0, 0x4B0, 'shared-mutable', 'the timedemo per-sample array. 0x22170 stores [ecx*4+0x7D67E0] at 221F7 only while the index 0x7D67B4 < 0x12C (221EF): 300 dwords. Read by the fps report 0x21F90 (22043, 220D0; "fps.txt", "%d Min/Max"). 22170 is called from 0x5CFF0, which _Host_Frame calls at 5D566, after the last turn: once per process frame. [review 96]'),
