    (0x3AAD48, 0x3680, 'shared-mutable', '32 entries of 0x1B4: 0x20220 shifts them up (source = dest-0x1B4, 0x6D dwords, from 0x3AE214 = 0x3AAD48+31*0x1B4 down while >= 0x3AAEFC, 0x20221..0x20270) and writes entry 0 (rep movsd 0x6D dwords to 0x3AAD48, 0x2027A..0x20284; fixups 0x20287..0x2029B). 0x1DEB0 (from V_RenderView 0xB5E90) walks entries 1..30 (0x1DFCC cmp 0x1F, imul 0x1B4 at 0x1DFD5). The only writer chain is 0x202B0 <- 0x2280D in the demo reader 0x22940: written only during demo playback, never in a split-screen match, and read only in the render path (player 1). Per client by nature (demo state), but not changed in M2; swapping 13.9 KB per switch buys nothing. Correction to the batch: the extent is 0x3680 (0x3AAD48..0x3AE3C8), not 0x1B4. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x3AE3C8, 0x8, 'player', 'two dwords set together at 0x2402F/0x24035 from [esp+0x10] (from cls.netchan 0x781324) and cls.netchan.incoming_sequence [0x781320] (0x24029); read at 0x23D6C (cmp with the new sequence+1), 0x23ECA and 0x23F87 to compute the latency/loss over the frames between. Only exact dword accesses (who 3AE3C0..3AE3D4). Derived from this client\\\'s own netchan (cls, per player), in CL_ParseClientdata 0x30900 ("clientdata_t"), so per client. Not the same object as [19] (different writer) nor predicted_players 0x3AE3D0. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x3AEA88, 0x100, 'shared-mutable', '0x29220 (from CL_SendConnectPacket 0x29310) clears the buffer: 0x3DA50 with ecx=0x100, edx=0x3AEA88 (0x292A5..0x292B1), copies at most 0xFF chars of the MD5 hex (esi=0xFF, 0x292BA..0x292E2), writes the terminator at 0x3AEA88+0xFF (0x292F3) and returns 0x3AEA88 (0x292F9) to its caller, which uses it at once. Static return buffer rewritten before every use. 0x3AEB88/0x3AEB8C are a different object (the rcon address, console 0x2A280). [review 2/0]'),
    (0x3AEEE4, 0x4, 'player', "in 0x321C0, a pmove sound callback installed by CL_RunUsercmd (0x32270/0x32310 stored at 0x3298F..0x329A3): delta = cl.time [0x74A290] - [0x3AEEE4] -> 0x5518C4 (0x321D6..0x321E8), then [0x3AEEE4] = cl.time (0x321EE/0x321F4). Exact dword float accesses only. It holds this client\\'s cl.time, so per client. [review 2/0]"),
    (0x3AEEE8, 0xC, 'player', 'the previous smoothed predicted origin in CL_PredictMove 0x32EB0: read 0x334AB..0x334C3 (fsub), 0x334E1..0x33503 (fld, added to the error terms into cl.simorg 0x74A144..0x74A14C), written 0x33524..0x3352F from 0x74A144..0x74A14C. Three exact dwords. Prediction smoothing of one client. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x3AEEF4, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'CL_PushPMStates 0x33550 saves pmove [0x552C34]+0x240 and +0x22828 (0x3356C..0x3357E) and sets the depth flag 0x5518DC=1 (0x33584); CL_PopPMStates 0x33590 restores them (0x335AC..0x335BE) and decrements the flag (0x335C4). Each push is popped in the same function: 0x2ADA6/0x2ADE4 in CL_Move 0x2AC80 and 0x33026/0x33144 in 0x32EB0. Scratch within one call, like pmove itself. Must share the ownership of the flag 0x5518DC and of pmove 0x552C34. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x3AEF00, 0x762A0, 'player', "tempent pool: 250 TEMPENTITY of 0x790 (cl_entity_t 0x74C at +0x44). mov ecx, 0x1D8A8; rep stosd at 3A8AA/3A8AF; link loop next = +0x2C, stride 0x790, bound 0x424A3C (3A8C0..3A8D6). Init 0x3A8A0 runs from CL_ClearState at 28EE1 on each connect (0x2E780) and once at start-up from 0x33DE0 <- CL_Init. Entries are allocated by 3A950/3A9C0 with cl.time 0x74A290 (3A90D). They are updated through HUD_TempEntUpdate from CL_EmitEntities (2659C -> 3AF20) in each player\\'s frame. Shared would mean player 2\\'s connect wipes player 1\\'s tempents and both clients age one list with their own times. Large: about 0.5 MB per swap. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x4251A0, 0x8, 'player', 'free head 0x4251A0 and active head 0x4251A4 (3A8DB/3A8E5; alloc 3A951..3A9AA, 3A9C1..3AA19; 3AA3C..3AA76; passed by address at 3AF42/3AF47). Must have the same ownership as the pool 0x3AEF00 and gTempEntFrame 0x5BDA5C. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x430810, 0x1000, 'shared-mutable', '0x3DEE0 (format "%02x") clears 0x400 dwords at 0x430810 (0x3DEF2..0x3DF05), appends 2 hex chars per byte with a 0xFFF limit (0x3DF3A..0x3DF4C), returns 0x430810 (0x3DF5F). Callers 0x29310 (connect packet), 0x2D580 (resource list) use it at once. Scratch rewritten before every use. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x43A8EC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', '0x4E4C0 (R_Clear, 5 GL-table calls; glClear [0x6A8C8C] 0x4E534) increments it (0x4E53A..0x4E542) and picks the depth range by its low bit (0x4E540 test al,1; 0x4E549 sets gldepthmin 0x6CE200). Mirrors the one depth buffer. Render path (0x4D300, 0x4EF00 R_RenderView). [review 2/0]'),
    (0x43AC90, 0x20D0, 'shared-mutable', "gDecalPool: R_DecalInit 0x53020 clears 0x834 dwords (0x5302A/0x5302F) = 300 x 0x1C; R_DecalAlloc 0x530F0 steps an index modulo r_decals (default 0x12C, 0x530FF; cvar 0x377304) with imul 0x1C + 0x43AC90 (0x53139/0x5313C); 0x53160 / 0x531C0 walk 0x43AC90..0x43CD60 by 0x1C (0x531AD/0x531B0). 0x53160 is reached from the server too (role server). Decals sit in the shared world surfaces\\' chains (docs table: one decal pool, applied once). [review 2/0]"),
    (0x43CD78, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "gDecalCount, the pool\\'s index: cleared by 0x53020 (0x53031), read/written by 0x530F0 (0x53122, 0x5314D). Must share the pool\\'s ownership. [review 2/0]"),
    (0x43E108, 0x4, 'process', '0x5E410 (a _Host_Frame step) sets it once: only if 0 (0x5E410..0x5E41A), from the time 0xAC240 (0x5E41C..0x5E426). Read only by the stats command 0x5E530 ("Uptime", fisub at 0x5E6E5). Set once, then constant; whichever turn sets it first, the value is the same clock. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x440BB0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', '0x6DFE0 ("%.1f fps", "in :  %i %.2f k/s", "loss: %i choke:  %i") keeps the last non-zero value (0x6E196..0x6E1A2). Called only by 0x6E4B0, called only by SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10, which an added player skips. Display of player 1 only in M2. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x448A70, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'smoothed in/out rates in 0x6E4B0 ("in_graph", "%i/s"): x = (x + v) * k (0x6E5C9..0x6E5D5), read for display 0x6EB12. 0x6E4B0 is called only from SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10. Display of player 1 in M2; a per-viewport net graph later is host-side (docs table). [review 2/0]'),
    (0x448AB8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the same smoothing (0x6E5E7..0x6E5F3), read 0x6EB07. Same function, same reason. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x448ABC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'net_configured: NET_Config 0x691A0 tests ==1 (0x691A0) and sets 1 (0x691B0); the console commands 0x29CD0, 0x2A280, 0x64A50 and 0x6D380 write it. The one network layer (pairs with 0x378854, cluster [8]). [review 2/0]'),
    (0x49F684, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', '0x85FA0 (particle tracer/streak effect) reads it (0x862D5), uses bit 2 for the colour (0x862F4..0x86300), increments it (0x86316/0x8631F) and alternates the streak scale by bit 0 (0x86317, 0x86327). Cosmetic, inside the particle system whose allocator heads 0x49F67C / 0x49F688 are reviewed shared (review 0). [review 2/0]'),
    (0x4E50B0, None, 'shared-mutable', 'a session/validation state machine ("CL_ISMV"; state 0x4E50B8, double timer 0x4E50D8, buffer 0x4E50E0). The server drives it in its own frames: A1D20 -> A6FF0 -> B2CA0/B2E10/B33A0 (B2DBC, B316A, B33F5), and the connectionless handler 9BE50 -> B2890 (B29EA..B2C68). It cannot be per-player: a swapped copy would hand the server whichever player was swapped in last. Extent not proven (indexed read at B2BF0). Open risk: each client\\\'s CL_ParseServerInfo (2EE42) and 0x297D0 call 0xB24E0, which resets it (state=7 at B252D). An added player\\\'s connect may disturb player 1\\\'s exchange. Needs a runtime check. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5255CC, 0x20, 'shared-mutable', "three vec3 (0x5255CC, 0x5255E0, 0x5255F8; 9 dwords), written by 0xB5D10 from the client\\'s ref_params (+0x18..+0x38, 0xB5D45..0xB5D90) and read into the next ref_params by 0xB5AB0 (0xB5AEF..0xB5B33). Both are called only from V_RenderView 0xB5E90 (0xB5F14, 0xB6012), whose chain is 0xB4560 <- 0xB55E0 <- SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10: never run in an added player\\'s turn in M2. Note for per-viewport rendering later: they are written by the same instructions as r_refdef 0x6E7A90.. (0xB5D12..0xB5D3F), so they must then follow r_refdef\\'s ownership.; trimmed to 0x20 (the view vectors), 0x5255EC is its own entry [review 2/0]"),
    (0x5255EC, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'V_CheckGamma 0xB5960 compares 0x5255EC/F0/F4 and 0x525608 with gamma cvars 0x37A1A4/0x37A190/0x37A1B8/0x37A1CC (0xB5960..0xB59B2), rebuilds the gamma table (0xB59BD call 0xB56A0), stores them (0xB59D3..0xB59F2) and sets 0x6CE2CC=1. Called from SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10 and 0xB5A00. One display gamma. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x525608, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the fourth saved gamma value (0xB598A, 0xB59DF). Same function. [review 2/0]'),
    (0x527280, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'voice record timestamp: double. Written by 102250 (fstp 1022B3 after Sys_FloatTime AC240; this function also creates the record buffers 5526F4/552700 with malloc 1022C3/1022ED) and by 102440 (fld 1024B2 / fstp 10250E). The voice functions 101EB0/101F40/101FD0 ("Voice - chan %d"), 102760 ("incoming samples added to channel") and 102350 drive one microphone/mixer through the interface pointers 5526E8/5526EC (calls [edx+0x14] 102279, [eax+0x04] 101F15). One device, so it is the sound subsystem. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5432C8, 0x4, 'player', "cam_thirdperson: set by the camera commands 18C0A0@18C0CB, 18C100@18C107, 1A5DE0@1A5DE7, read by CAM_Think 18BA60@18BA97, 18C3B0@18C3B0, 18C450@18C450, 18C4F0 (CL_IsThirdPerson) and 1B83B0. Each local client's own view mode. [review 2/ut_32]"),
    (0x5432CC, 0x4, 'player', 'cam_old_mouse_y; 0x54330C cam_old_mouse_x: 18C3B0@18C41D/18C413, 18C450@18C4B3/18C4A9, 18BA60@18BCD0/18BCC4 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x54330C, 0x4, 'player', 'see above [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543310, 0x4, 'player', 'cam_distancemove: 18C450@18C475, 18C4D0@18C4D2, read 18BA60@18BAD1 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543330, 0x4, 'player', 'cam_mousemove: 18C3B0@18C3D5, 18C440@18C442, 18C450@18C47A, 18C4D0@18C4D7 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543334, 0x8, 'player', 'cam_mouse.x/y (two dwords: 543334 and 543338, set to 0x140/0xF0 at 18C484/18C48E, read throughout 18BA60) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5433E0, 0x4, 'player', 'HUD_WeaponsPostThink 18E430@18ED2A: (~[esi+0x290] & 2) >> 1 from this client predicted state. Written per prediction call by the client own prediction (18F330 HUD_PostRunCmd -> 18E430). Per-player: the result of that client prediction. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543634, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x54364C, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543658, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543664, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543688, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x5436C4, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x5436D8, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543704, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543718, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543774, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543788, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x543794, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x5437A4, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x5437B0, 0xC, 'player', "kbutton_t {down[2], state}: KeyDown 0x18F820 / KeyUp 0x18F880 use +0/+4/+8 through esi = this address; CL_ButtonBits 0x190550 tests and clears its state from each player's CL_CreateMove [review 2/32]"),
    (0x5437D8, 0x4, 'player', 'IN_Init 19E660 sets it to 0; joystick state [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5437DC, 0x1, 'player', 'IN_JoyMove 19E160 rumble-active flag: set 19E35F, cleared 19E3BC, read 19E47D. It mirrors whether this client has started the force-feedback effect on 0x5CBBA8 (call C82E0 at 19E334). [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5437EC, 0x10, 'player', 'four dwords 5437EC..5437F8 cleared by 19DF70 (19DF77..19DF95): joystick axis flags; pairs with 543A20 ([36]) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543800, 0x4, 'player', 'IN_Init 19E660 sets it to 1 (joystick present/enabled) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5439A4, 0x4, 'player', 'IN_JoyMove 19E160 state: written 19E55D, read 19E428; IN_Init clears it [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5439D4, 0x4, 'player', 'IN_Init 19E660 sets 1 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5439DC, 0x10, 'player', 'dwAxisMap: 19DF70 stores 3,1,4,2 at 19DF9A..19DFB8 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5439FC, 0x4, 'player', "IN_Init 19E660 sets 0'); (0x543A10, 0x4, 'player', 'IN_Init 19E660 sets 0 [review 2/ut_32]"),
    (0x543A18, 0x4, 'player', 'IN_JoyMove 19E160: written 19E551, read 19E3D3; IN_Init clears it [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543A20, 0x10, 'player', 'four dwords cleared by 19DF70 (19DF72..19DF90) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543A3C, 0x1, 'player', 'IN_JoyMove rumble flag: 19E32E set, 19E3B5 clear, read 19E316/19E41F; same caveat as 5437DC [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543A50, 0x1C, 'player', 'seven dwords 543A50..543A68 written by the client demo-buffer reader 19EB20 ("Unknown demo buffer type", 19EB40..19EB8C) from the demo stream: view values of the client playing a demo. Low stakes (only a demo-playing client writes them) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x543A78, 0x4, 'player', 'mouse sensitivity scale: 1BAF80@1BAFEE fstp right after 1AE430 ("zoom_sensitivity_ratio"), reached from the client export 18B870; console 19EF50 resets it to 1.0f. This client zoom state. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x545A70, 0x46, 'shared-mutable', 'XINPUT_FEEDBACK (header dwStatus/hEvent + 58 reserved bytes, then XINPUT_RUMBLE at +0x42): its address is pushed to XInputSetState 0x3196E3 (analysis/game_5849sigs_experiment.toml:239) by 1A7BF0 (push 0x545A70 at 1A7C43). Rumble words at +0x42/+0x44 = 545AB2/545AB4 (1A7C0E/1A7C14, word access), hEvent +4 = 545A74 (1A7C04). The size comes from the XDK struct and matches the +0x42/+0x44 word fields; no instruction bounds the reserved bytes. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x545AB8, 0x46, 'shared-mutable', 'second XINPUT_FEEDBACK: pushed at 1A7C50/1A7C5E then call 3196E3 at 1A7C64; hEvent 545ABC (1A7FF8), rumble 545AFA/545AFC (1A7FFE/1A8005) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x548738, 0xC, 'player', 'three dwords. 18C5E0 (HUD_TxferLocalOverrides-type export) copies them from the client own entity state; 18B970 clears all three (mov [..],ebx); 1A9480 (spectator SetModes "specmode %i") writes 548738; 1B09A0 writes 54873C/548740; 1AF270 (jointeam) writes 548740=1. Each local client has its own spectator mode/target. The only non-client reader is the Xbox UI CA3D0 (CA446..CA4DC reads 548740), which runs in player 1 turn. Already a region (client_context_regions.inc:117). [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x548E58, 0x4, 'player', 'serial counter: 1BAC30 reads at 1BAC7E, stores the value in the effect record [edi+0x18] (1BAC9A), increments and writes back at 1BACA0, then passes it to an engine API call [eax+0x08] of [0x543240] (1BACAD). It numbers this client own effect list (esi+0x410). Per-player is consistent. The stakes are low. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x548E5C, 0x4, 'player', '1BAF80@1BAFCF from the input record [edi+0x1C]; write-only (no reader), so harmless whatever its class [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x548E60, 0x4, 'player', 'HUD_Init 18B800@18B824; write-only [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x548E64, 0x10, 'player', 'four dwords 548E64..548E70 set by the grid init 1CC5D0 (1CC609..1CC62E: 3000.0f, 0, 1000.0f, 0) and read by 18F570 (18F579..18F5AF) and 1CC682. They belong with the per-player particle grid 0x57F0A8 that 1CC5D0 clears (region_evidence.py:197), and 1CC5D0 runs from each player own initialisation (18B970/1A5EE0). [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551790, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'scratch: 1DC0C0 stores the COM_LoadFile result ([0x543224] at 1DC14B) at 1DC15D. Its only reader is 1F6920@1F6921, called at 1DC163 (1F6920 has no other caller). The buffer is then freed by [0x54322C] at 1DC169. Rewritten before every use. The value left behind is a dangling heap pointer that nothing reads. If it is kept in a region, the scrub sees a stale heap pointer. Harmless either way. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5517F8, 0x10, 'player', "CMiniMem pool sizes and blocks (1F9B90, 1F9F80, 1FAA40). DECISION (docs 14.5): the client game's particle manager (CMiniMem / IParticleMan) is a player's as a whole: each player's Initialize makes its own (0x18B7A0 -> 0x18B710 -> 0x1F8E40 -> 0x1F9EC0, the object 0x552B8C, the pool 0x5517F8), so its lists, pool-chunk vector and grid follow it (the fourth run's blocked free 0x1815DE: vector shared, pool per-player)"),
    (0x551808, 0x8, 'player', 'particle manager clock: double. Set by 1F9F80@1FA103, accumulated by 1FAA40 (fadd/fst 1FAC5E/1FAC64), only these two access it. It belongs with the per-player particle manager (0x552B8C/0x552CE4, docs 10.4). Note: REVIEWED_FUNCTIONS marks the CMiniMem allocators 1F9B90.. as shared. That conflicts with the docs keeping 0x552CE4 per-player. Reconcile one way for the whole particleman. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551824, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: the water XPR texture handles from 152D0 ("waterplain.xpr", 1537E) and 551828; read by 15B58. D3D resources on the one device [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x55182C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'renderer: 4EF00 (R_RenderView speeds, gl=1) stores (int)x mod 0x11 at 4EF9B (idiv ecx=0x11), read by 15A4D [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551868, 0x8, 'player', 'demo playback state 551868/55186C: CL_ReadDemoMessage 22449/22940 (226A7, 22754, 227C9) under cls 0x785580 == 1. Same owner as cls [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551884, 0x8, 'player', 'CL_ParsePacketEntities byte accounting: 242F0 adds (243F0) and keeps the maximum in 551888 (243F7); 23740 subtracts at 23752 before free 0x22C609 at 23758. It counts this client own entity allocations [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551898, 0x8, 'player', 'CL_SendConnectPacket 29310@2936B: Sys_FloatTime of the connect attempt; write-only [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518A8, 0x1, 'player', 'download/signon flag: CL_ProcessFile 285F0@287AB, 297D0 (read 297DC, write 298B7), CL_ParseServerInfo 2E780@2ED54/2ED95/2EDBA/2EE5A. Each client connection [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518B0, 0x4, 'process', 'count of the start-sound queue 0x749400 (50 x 0x24, reviewed process, region_evidence.py:274): bound cmp ecx,0x32 at 2F37D, entry = count*0x24 (2F386/2F389), increment stored at 2F3DA. It must share the queue ownership. The scan files it under 30E50 (a jmp to 2F160). It is written only while [0x5518A4]==0, i.e. before start-up completes. src/game/client_context_regions.inc:128 currently swaps 0x5518B0+0x10: remove 5518B0 from that region. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518B4, 0x4, 'player', 'index of the svc history 0x3AEBA0 (reviewed player, region_evidence.py:106): incremented at 3039B, used with and 0x1F at 30371 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518B8, 0x8, 'player', 'client clock-drift accumulator (double): 30700 (fld 30709..307D9, fstp 307E1, 308B0, 308C9), the client half of the host frame. Uses this client cl.time 0x74A290. 30820 is CL_ParseTime (reads net_message at 748404, writes cl.mtime 0x74A280/0x74A288) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518C0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'head of the event-hook list. CL_HookEvent 0x31D40 looks up the name first (0x31CC0) and only replaces the handler if found (31D83); otherwise it adds a node of 0xC (31D88..31DAF). Freed by 0x31DD0 and zeroed by Host_Init (5DC6A). A registry of names to the same functions, like the user-message list 0x5518AC. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5518C4, 0x4, 'player', '321C0@321E8: cl.time 0x74A290 minus the stored time 0x3AEEE4 (already a region, client_context_regions.inc:50) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518CC, 0x4, 'player', 'CL_PredictMove 32EB0 loop index (3305A, 33134; bound [0x371CF0]-1 at 33055). Effectively scratch per call. Harmless as player [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518D0, 0x8, 'player', 'prediction timing (double): 323B0@32555 ("pred. error"), 32EB0 (333CC..33499) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518D8, 0x4, 'player', '323B0: counter whose value &3 +10 picks the Con_NPrintf line (324A1..324B8). Cosmetic [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518DC, 0x4, 'player', 'CL_PushPMStates 33550 sets 1 (33584) after checking it (33550), CL_PopPMStates 33590 checks and decrements (335C4). Balanced inside one prediction call [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5518E4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'cmd_functions head: Cmd_AddCommand 0x3C760, its variant 0x3C8C0 (from the client-game pfnAddCommand 0x1BFD0), 0x3C990 and the shutdown 0x5DDA0. Read by the command executor (3CA10, server) and the console (3CCD0). One command registry. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x551910, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'console-visible flag: Con_ToggleConsole 0x40630 (setz at 4063A/4063D), Con_IsVisible 0x40620, the console draw 0x40920/0x40970, Key_Event 0x66510 (66751), SV_SpawnServer A066A and 40AAA. One console and keyboard. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x551960, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'text-draw colour index: read 469CE as index into the colour table 0x741EE0 (469D4). Set by the screen/net-graph draw code 56180 (from SCR_UpdateScreen 55E10: 56195, 5628F..56307), 47060@47108, 6D7E0@6D829 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551964, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'sprite scissor rect x,y,w,h,enabled (5 dwords 551964..551974): 472B0 sets them and enabled=1 (47308..4731F), 231D0 clears all five (231D8..231EC). Read by sprite draw (47484/474C3). Only the drawing player uses it, inside its own HUD draw [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551994, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', '229C0 (an engine function handed to the client) stores its argument at 229D2. Read by the lightmap code R_BuildLightMap 4FE45, 505A7, 50B47, R_BlendLightmaps 51000, 58D13: renderer state [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x55199C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'lightmap allocation state: GL_BuildLightmaps 529C0 (52DAA, 53001), read 505E1/51187/51536: renderer (gl=7) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551CC4, 0x8, 'player', 'SCR_CenterPrint 55180: current (551CC4, 5521E) and previous (551CC8, 55218) localized-string pointers. 55790 clears 551CC8 (55836). 55180 is called from this client svc parse handlers (30A70/31060/31090) and the client engfunc 1C5B0. Each local client receives its own centre prints. Already a region (regions.inc:134). [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551DA8, 0x20, 'shared-mutable', 'host statistics computed by 5E410 (from _Host_Frame 5D2E0): 551DA8 (double FPS, 5E4C8), 551DB0 (5E518), 551DB4 (5E50D), 551DB8/551DBC (5E501/5E507), 551DC0/551DC4 (5E476/5E47C, 5E4F6/5E4FB) from the host frame counters 0x6CDFE0/4. The only reader of 551DA8 is the "stats" console command 5E530 (5E719). Process-wide diagnostics. Running in two turns only changes the statistic. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551DE4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'Key_Event 66510: state of key 0x86 (665F4/665FC), read 6677A. The one key system [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551DF0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'key_dest 0x551DF0 and the chat length 0x551DF4 of the one keyboard handler. Key_Message 0x65B90 (65BA4/65BAA, 65BE2/65BFB, 65C3F/65C45) and the console commands 0x5F520/0x65ED0 write them. Key_Event 0x66510, SCR_UpdateScreen, the view and the server (A1D76, ABA3A) read them. The added player reads no keys.; trimmed to 4, 0x551DF4 is its own entry [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x551DF4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'chat message mode (65B90 "say": length/state 551DF0/551DF4 with buffer 0x6CA740, 65BA4..65C45; console 65ED0@65F25). The one key_dest/chat UI in M2 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551E1C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "the network layer\\'s IP-enabled flag: NET_GetLocalAddress 0x6D150 (6D29A) and the network init 0x6D530 (6D629). Read by NET_Config callers and server code (9A4A5, 9AB53). [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x551E20, None, 'shared-mutable', 'ip_sockets[]: NET_OpenIP 0x6CFD0 (6D0EB/6D103). Indexed by socket type in NET_QueuePacket 0x6C340 (6C363) and NET_SendPacket 0x6CC70 (6CCD1/6CCE7). One network layer; extent not proven here. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x551E24, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'NET_Config 6CFD0 ("NET Ports", 6D04E), read 6D006/6D27D: network layer [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551E6C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'network-configured flag: 6D380@6D402/6D435 (setnz), 691A0@691D9, connect/rcon commands 29E81/2A3A0/64A9F. The one network layer [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551E70, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'net-graph flag: 6E4B0 (from SCR_UpdateScreen, "in_graph") sets 1 at 6E519, 6EB46 clears it, read by the UI B9816/B9D06/B9F5F. Drawing state [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551EF0, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', '551EF4 = array malloc(ebx*8) by 93180 ("Transparent objects reallocate", 931A0/931B0), 551EF0 = its capacity (931B6). Read by the renderer (93340, 93421, 93536, 93570, 9364B, 9381F). Freed and zeroed by CL_Disconnect 28F20 (free 2907C; 29084/2908A) and by 2E2A0 under CL_ParseServerInfo (2E2CD/2E2D3). The allocation follows each client connect/disconnect. If it stayed shared, an added player disconnect at 2907C would free the array player 1 renderer is using. Per-player keeps each lifecycle separate (player 2 copy is never drawn in M2). It holds a heap pointer: scrub. Alternative: keep it shared and skip 2E2A0/28F20 freeing in added players turns. Either way 551EF0 and 551EF4 share one owner.. DECISION: shared: the renderer\'s transparent-object array (0x93180, its blocks SharedScratch in native_split.cpp kSiteRules), used by the drawing only player 1 does in M2 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x551F9C, 0x4, 'player', 'connection flag written beside cls fields (2D844..2D854 with cls.state 0x7812E0=4), 27AE0@27B59, CL_CheckForResend 298F0@29936, 3DF70@3DFD1, connect command 29CD0@29E3E. Write-only (no reader), so harmless whatever its class [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552044, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'front-end object field set by B9300 (caller B9490); B9180 is a constructor (callers include static init 23CD40/23CD60) of the front-end objects (docs 10.4: front end shared until M4) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552048, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'front-end setting byte: B9180, menus DAD40/DB770 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552049, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'font loaded flag: BC900 ("d:\\\\media\\\\fonts\\\\", "_IdHudFont.xpr") sets 1. The font is one renderer resource. BC900 is reached from client HUD code and engine draw 47060 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552058, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'UI byte: BDFC0/BE13D (from UI C2160) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5520A0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'C3E90 (map texture load, "d:\\\\media\\\\textures\\\\%s.xpr", "%s_detail.xpr") frees the old name buffer (C3F47..C3F60), mallocs a new one (C4042/C404E), and loads the XPR into the bundle 0x553E78 (C406B call C4E80). Then the detail textures 13C60 (C4083) and more. Renderer resources on one device. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552318, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the zone allocator\\\'s byte count: every Z_Malloc/Z_Free site does read, add/subtract and store ("ZONE alloc (%d bytes) - now %d"): 1BF06/1BF19, 3BA54/3BA65, 3C630/3C648, 4214E/42162, 42441, 65D62, C8E71, C8EA6... Allocator statistics, like 0x3820D0. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x552346, 0x1, 'player', 'buy-zone flag written by the client HUD status-icon code 1D7850@1D7862 (=1) and 1D79B0@1D79EF (from message handlers 1A5F40/1D7720). Read only by the Xbox UI: CD7D0@CD824 (UI frame from SCR_UpdateScreen) and CA830@CA844. The value is this client message data. Swapped, the UI drawn in player 1 turn reads player 1 value. Shared, player 2 message would change player 1 buy menu. It is a byte inside a UI-owned group: 552344 and 552345 are written by the UI (BF470 startup, C9FC0, D88E0..D91C0) and stay shared. Exact byte accesses only, so a 1-byte region is valid. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552348, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'UI buy-menu state: written by the UI CA550@CA585, CACD0@CAE0E/CAE5A and the client buy command E62C0@E6342 (caller 18FCB0), read by UI CA3D0. The menus are shared until M4 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5523E8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'HUD font loader BC900 (xpr font resource); same subsystem as 552049 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5526B8, 0x6D, 'shared-mutable', 'voice state written only by the voice functions: 1029F0/102A80 (record start/stop, 5526B8, 5526BC), 101EB0 (Voice_Deinit: releases [0x5526EC]/[0x5526E8]/[0x5526BC] through their vtables 101EFC/101F15/101F2E, clears 5526B9/5526E8/5526EC), 101F40/101FD0 (Voice_Idle, doubles 5526C0..5526D8, 5526E0/E4), 102250/102350/102440/102760 (record buffers 5526F4/552700 malloc 1022C3/1022ED, positions 5526F8/552704/552714), 103370 (55271C/552720), 102620/101FD0 (552724). One microphone and mixer. Each member keeps its own access width. The group is listed as one range only because it all has one owner. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552B80, 0x8, 'player', 'Initialize 18B7A0 zeroes 552B80/552B84 (18B7CF/18B7D4); write-only [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552B8C, 0x4, 'player', 'particle manager pointer, made by Initialize -> 18B710 / 1F8E40, deleted by 18B830. Per-player heap object (docs 10.4, scrub) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552B90, 0x4, 'player', 'iMouseInUse: the camera commands 18C3B0@18C3DC, 18C440@18C447, 18C450@18C47F, 18C4D0@18C4DC. Same owner as [33] [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552B98, 0x4, 'process', 'num_ents of HUD_PrepEntity 0x18D550 (inc / store at 18D57C/18D57F). Its only caller, and the only other writer (18E248/18E254), is HUD_InitClientWeapons 0x18E160 (calls at 18E274..18E427). That function runs under the once-flag 0x5BDA60 (process). Nothing else reads it (who.py), so it goes with that flag. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x552B9C, 0x1, 'player', 'HUD_WeaponsPostThink 18E430@18ED3C: bit 2 of the predicted flags. Read later by the HUD draw code 1C2930@1C2978 and 1CEF20@1CEF68/1CF3D7, in a different call. Unlike 552BA8 (reviewed as per-call shared-mutable), it is consumed outside the call, so it must be per-player [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BA0, 0x8, 'player', 'HUD_PostRunCmd 18F330@18F38A/18F392; read by 192590 (1925FB/19260C) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BA9, 0x1, 'player', '18E430 sets 0/1 (18ED94, 18EE25: [edx+0xB8]==2), read by HUD 1D1270@1D12C9/1D1A55 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BAC, 0x4, 'player', 'in_impulse: the impulse command 18FDC0 (Cmd_Argv(1) via [0x543184], atoi 22C9B6, 18FDD1). CL_CreateMove 190150 reads it at 190317 and clears it at 190329 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BB0, 0x4, 'player', 'jlook-type flag: 18FDA0 releases kbutton 0x54369C (KeyUp 18F880) and clears it at 18FDAB. CL_ButtonBits 190550 reads it at 19059D (adds 0x40) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BB4, 0x4, 'player', 'heap object, per docs 10.4 (18F790 under InitInput, 190690@... =0, console 190CA0 =0) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BB8, 0x4, 'player', 'gHUD.Init 1A65A0@1A69EE (registered cvar/pointer), read 192B05, 1D5C18. Rewritten by each HUD_Init [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552BC4, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'vector end/cap-type fields built by the client lightmap callback 195770 (195B39/195B69), reached only from the renderer: GL_BuildLightmaps 529C0 -> 196160, and 51900 -> 196240 (gl=2). Same owner as 56D598.. ([59]) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C10, 0x8, 'player', 'two view-angle accumulators 552C10/552C14: IN_JoyMove 19E160 adds and clamps them (19E4C3..19E52E) and IN_Init zeroes them. svc parse handler 30AB0 (reads net_message 748404/6BA588) sets them, and the UI CA150@CA172/CA178 when the buy menu closes. Each client input/angle state. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C28, 0x8, 'player', 'demo-buffer reader 19EB20 (19EB4B/19EB5F), as 543A50 ([36]) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C30, 0x4, 'process', 'once-flag of the shared player-movement init: 18B6C0 (HUD_PlayerMoveInit) tests it (18B6C0), stores pmove 552C34, calls 1A5850 and PM_InitTextureTypes 1A1140, then sets 1 (18B6DC). The server side does the same at 5E14D..5E161. It guards process-wide state (552C38/552C40 reviewed process, 552C34 shared-mutable), so it must share their owner. A per-player copy would re-run PM_InitTextureTypes against the process copy. That is harmless only because of 552C40 own guard. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C54, 0xC, 'player', 'gHUD.Init 1A65A0 stores 552C54, 552C58 and 552C60 (registered cvars, read e.g. 1DC1C5 [eax+0x0C]); 552C5C is not touched. Rewritten by each HUD_Init [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C64, 0x4, 'player', 'prediction float: HUD_PostRunCmd 18F330 (18F365 read, 18F3F0/18F403 write), 1A71E0 (1A71F7..1A723D), 1A7250@1A72E1 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C70, 0x4, 'player', 'force-feedback system object (deleted 1A7F82, malloc 0x48 1A7F8C, stored 1A7FDE). Per docs 10.4, heap, scrub. Console 190CA0 clears it. Its device buffers 545A70/545AB8 stay shared ([37]) [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C80, 0xC, 'player', 'weapon prediction outputs 552C80/552C84/552C88 from 18E430 (18EAE3, 18EA58, 18EB8C fsqrt speed), read by the HUD 1AD200 (1AD20D..1AD251) and 1AD3B0 (1AD4D8/1AD50C) outside the call [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552C8C, 0x4, 'player', "gHUD.Init 1A65A0, rewritten by each HUD_Init'); (0x552CB0, 0x4, 'player', 'gHUD.Init 1A65A0, same [review 2/ut_32]"),
    (0x552C9C, 0x4, 'player', 'loadconfig object (1B6670 under InitInput; console 190CA0 =0); per docs 10.4 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552CA8, 0x4, 'player', 'object freed and remade by 1BAE40 under gHUD.Init (docs 11.1); the atexit destructor 1A6C80 clears it [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552CAC, 0x1, 'player', 'grid init 1CC5D0 clears it (1CC627, 1CC659). Owned with the grid 0x57F0A8 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552CBC, 0x4, 'player', 'material parser cursor (COM_LoadFile result at 1DC138, COM_Parse loop 1DD2A0, cleared 1DC184). Rewritten before each use, so it is effectively scratch. Kept per-player by docs 10.4. Harmless [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552CCC, 0x4, 'player', 'material counter: 1F6920 sets it (1F6934) and increments it (1F69EA), read by 1DBFE0/1DC0C0/1F68B0. Goes with the material list made by each player own load (1DC0C0 <- 1AE430 <- 1BAF80 <- export 18B870). Unresolved whether the material list should be one process resource. If the list is shared, 552CCC must be too. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552CDC, 0x10, 'player', "cl_pmanstats cvar 0x552CDC (1F8E28), the maximum 0x552CE0 (0x118 at 1F8E2D), the singleton 0x552CE4 (1F9F09), the time 0x552CE8 (1FA159). DECISION (docs 14.5): the client game's particle manager (CMiniMem / IParticleMan) is a player's as a whole: each player's Initialize makes its own (0x18B7A0 -> 0x18B710 -> 0x1F8E40 -> 0x1F9EC0, the object 0x552B8C, the pool 0x5517F8), so its lists, pool-chunk vector and grid follow it (the fourth run's blocked free 0x1815DE: vector shared, pool per-player)"),
    (0x552D10, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'water renderer resources from 152D0 (five dwords 552D10..552D20, caller C3E90 map load): D3D textures. See the [49] hazard [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552DD0, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'CA670 stores the pad stick x/y (CA678, CA684). IN_JoyMove calls it with the physical pad values when a UI menu [0x5523D4] is up (19E1AE..19E1C8). UI state in M2 [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552E70, 0x14, 'player', 'five dwords written identically by the client command 18FCD0 (KeyDown 0x5437A4, then 200E2C time into 552E70/552E74, 552E78/552E7C=0, 552E80=1) and the UI command E6280. No reader at a fixed address: write-only as far as can be seen. Harmless as player. If a pointer reader is ever found it would decide the class. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x552F58, 0x20, 'shared-mutable', 'detail textures (13C60 "_detail.txt", 139A0 parse; caller C3E90): 552F58, 552F64, 552F6C..552F74. 552F6C/70/74 look like a std::vector (begin/end/cap) cleared by the atexit destructor 23F3D0. Renderer resource. See the [49] hazard [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5541CC, 0x28, 'shared-mutable', 'C59A0 (from 5D1E0, the host frame sound step) copies the listener origin and orientation vectors and two flag bytes into 5541CC..5541F0 (C59B4..C59F6). Read by the sound code C5B30 (callers 1011C0, 101930). One sound output. 5D1E0 feeds it from the renderer globals 0x6E8890/0x6E7FE0, so an added player turn would write player 1 view anyway. Still, skip 5D1E0 in added players turns with the rest of sound. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x56D598, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'vector begin/end/cap-type triple: 195770 stores end (195F5C after 134F0, add esi,0x10) and reads it at 1959E8/195F1B. The atexit destructor 23FFD0 frees [0x56D598] (23FFDA) and clears 56D59C (23FFEC). Reached only from the renderer (GL_BuildLightmaps 529C0 -> 196160; 51900 -> 196240). Renderer. The extent 0xC is inferred from the destructor touching 56D598/56D59C and the vector pattern, not from a size instruction. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x56D66C, 0x18, 'shared-mutable', 'six dwords written by 18E430 (18ECB0..18ECE1) from [0x552B94]-relative vectors, with no reader anywhere (who.py 56D620..56D6C8). Write-only. The trace start 0x56D684 and trace result 0x56D628 are passed to the player trace [edx+0x3C] (18ECF0/18ECFE) inside the same call. Any class is safe. Shared costs nothing. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x56D6C0, 0x4, 'player', 'written with constants by the event scripts 1E0610/1E0BD0/1E1180/1E1480/1E1760/1E2160/1E2730 (EV_ fire functions); no reader. Write-only, harmless [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x576C78, 0xF0, 'player', 'five entries of 0x30. Cleared whole by rep stosd ecx=0x3C dwords (=0xF0) at 1B0A97..1B0AA1 (1B09A0) and 1B9285..1B928F (1B9250, "Scoreboard"). Index: lea eax,[eax+eax*2]; shl 4 (*0x30) at 1CC5B1/1CC5B4 and 1CC504/1CC507, bound cmp eax,4; jnle at 1CC5A0/1CC4F9. Filled by the message parsers 1CC4A0 (READ_COORD 1D5E70 into +4/+8/+0xC, gHUD time 562438 into +0x14) and 1CC570, reached from the client message hooks 1A5EA0/1A5EC0. Read by the HUD 1D5310 (mov ebp,0x576C8C at 1D56DB). Each client own message data. [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x57F08C, 0x4, 'player', 'counter decremented by the grid particle code 1CD2C0@1CD3DB; no reader (write-only). Goes with the per-player grid (1CC5D0 initialises the block at 0x57EEF0 via 1CCBA0). Harmless [review 2/ut_32]'),
    (0x5BD8A8, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', "IParticleMan::SetVariables 0x1F8EF0 (a vtable method) stores 3 floats at 1F8F03/1F8F09/1F8F0F; the draw 0x1FAA40 reads them (1FACE5/1FACEE/1FACF9). The caller is HUD_TempEntUpdate 0x18CA50 (call [eax+0x0C] at 18CA90, passing v_right 0x562454..0x56245C). This is the singleton particle system: it goes with its list 0x5BD8D8 and CMiniMem 0x5BD8C4 (already shared-mutable). Each player\\'s update rewrites the vector before its own particle pass. Caveat: with one particle list, player 1 also draws the particles that player 2\\'s messages create. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x5BD8C4, 0x18, 'player', "the pool's list head 0x5BD8C4, the chunk vector 0x5BD8C8 (allocator word, begin/last/end 0x5BD8CC..0x5BD8D4), the second list 0x5BD8D8 (1F9B90..1F9E40). DECISION (docs 14.5): the client game's particle manager (CMiniMem / IParticleMan) is a player's as a whole: each player's Initialize makes its own (0x18B7A0 -> 0x18B710 -> 0x1F8E40 -> 0x1F9EC0, the object 0x552B8C, the pool 0x5517F8), so its lists, pool-chunk vector and grid follow it (the fourth run's blocked free 0x1815DE: vector shared, pool per-player)"),
    (0x5BD8E0, 0x40, 'shared-mutable', '4x4 matrix: mov ecx, 0x10; mov edi, 0x5BD8E0; rep movsd from [eax+0xCA0] of the D3D device (1FA0D3..1FA0E1) on every particle update 0x1F9F80. It is used straight after by D3DXMatrixMultiply 0x24073E (out 0x5BD920, 1FA0E9) and by the draw 0x1FAA40 (push 0x5BD8E0 at 1FAACE/1FAAFD). Renderer scratch, rewritten before every use. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD960, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'once-flag of 0x136A0 (read at 136A0, set at 136D0). It guards the creation of the D3D texture stored at 0x3A97D0 (13738); "Create texture failed"; called from the map media loader 0xC3E90. A renderer resource, so the flag shares ownership with 0x3A97D0. A per-player flag would make a second texture. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD964, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'std::use_facet cache _Psave: 0x18E20 reads it at 18E54 and stores the new facet at 18EDB, then registers it (call 0x22B94C at 18EE8). It goes with the facet id 0x5D45C0 ([69]) and the id counter 0x3A63B4. C++ runtime, process-wide. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD968, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'same for 0x18D20 (18D54/18DDB; id 0x5D45C4). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD96C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'same for 0x18A10 (18A44/18ACD; id 0x3A63BC). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD970, 0x1, 'shared-mutable', 'once-flag of the water texture loader 0x152D0 (read at 152D0, set at 152F9). It guards 0x552D10..0x552D20 and 0x551824 ("Water XPR load failed"); called from 0xC3E90. Renderer resource; it goes with them. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD988, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'cached render-target size in 0xBE1D0 (compares 0x5BD98C/0x5BD988 at BE288/BE290, stores them at BE2AC/BE2B2, then recreates the D3D surface through 0x30D310). Called from 0xBDFC0 <- 0xC2160 <- the view 0xB4560. Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD990, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', "the state of 0xBDFC0\\'s render-target state machine: 0, 1 or 2 (BE01B; BE02F/BE055/BE0DF). Same draw path. Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x5BD9C8, 0x8, 'player', 'the high-latency detector 0xE9660. It is called only from CL_ParseClientdata at 2409F with cls.latency 0x785614 (push at 2409E). 0x5BD9C8 is the last GetTickCount (lazy init at E9667/E966E; E969B). 0x5BD9CC is the time accumulated over the threshold (E9693/E96A7; reset at E96B4). Above 0x7D0 ms it opens the "HighLatency" UI 0xE9600 (E96A2/E96AF). Each client measures its own latency. If shared, a good-latency turn would reset the other client\\\'s accumulator. Risk: 0xE9600 runs a modal loop that calls SCR_UpdateScreen (E9644). An added player who gets there in its own turn would draw, against the M2 rule. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BD9D8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the pending delay of the stats-report timer 0xFC870 (FC8D4/FC8F2, store at FC90E). 0xFC870 is also called by the server game\\\'s round-end code (call at 144D78 in 0x144D30, from 0x144E20 "Round_End" / 0x147620), not only by the client RoundEnd/RoundWin handlers (1A616A, 1A6243, 1A6710, 1B5DBD). Its id 0x56169C (FC94E) is read by server code 0xFC690/0xFC710. One shared Xbox stats subsystem. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BDA5C, 0x4, 'player', "gTempEntFrame of HUD_TempEntUpdate 0x18CA50: mov eax,[0x5BDA5C]; inc eax; and eax, 0x1F; mov [0x5BDA5C], eax (18CACA..18CADE); compared with tempent fields at 18D336. Its only caller is CL_TempEntUpdate 0x3AF20 (through [0x7D6D2C] at 3AF29, set at 1C86C), from CL_EmitEntities at 2659C, which runs in each player\\'s frame. It goes with the tempent lists (ubatch [1]). [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x5BDA64, 0x4, 'player', 'weapon-input timer of 0x190400 (weapon_c4; from 0x190550 <- CL_CreateMove-side 0x190150 and 0x1BAF80): fstp at 1904B7, fld at 1904DC. Its siblings 0x54369C..0x5436A4 (kbutton, already player) are cleared under it at 1904F4..19050C. Per-player input. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BDA68, 0x4, 'player', 'same function: fstp at 19047F/1904A8, fld at 190506/190519, cleared at 190528. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5BDA90, 0x1, 'player', "stick-deflection latch in the pad look code 0x19E160 (from 0x190150): set at 19E419 above a threshold, cleared at 19E450, read at 19E486 with 0x5437DC. Per-player input. If shared, the added player\\'s turn (it reads no pad) would clear player 1\\'s latch every frame. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x5C9648, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'the timer struct used with 0x5C9640 (esi=0x5C9640 at FC8E8; 0xC82E0 reads +8/+C start, +10/+14 accumulated and +18 running, at C82E3..C8311). FC870 writes 5C9648..5C9658 (FC899..FC8B1, FC920..FC944). Called from the server game (144D78) as well as the client: shared (see 0x5BD9D8). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5C9660, 0x4, 'process', 'the guard bit of the same static (test al,1 at FC87B; or edx,1 / store at FC889/FC88D). Under it only the frequency reciprocal 0x5C9640 (already process) is set, at FC8C6. It goes with 0x5C9640. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5C9C70, 0x1F00, 'shared-mutable', 'CSchemeManager ctor 0x1BB190: static 64 x 0x7C array (eh-vector-ctor push 0x40/0x7C/0x5C9C70 at 1BB218..1BB22C, under the guard 0x5CBB70). Each call clears it (mov ecx, 0x7C0; mov edi, 0x5C9C70; rep stosd at 1BB247..1BB255), fills it from *_textscheme.txt (loop bound cmp ebx, 0x5CBB70 at 1BB2B0) and consumes it in the same call (1BB77A). The only other accesses are its atexit dtor 0x240120 and the EH unwind 0x239550. Scratch, rewritten before every use. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5D34C8, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'last-time float 0x5D34C8 and its guard 0x5D34CC of the render-target code 0xBDFC0 (BDFFA..BE016, BE0F6/BE0FD). Renderer (see 0x5BD990). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5D34D4, 0xC, 'player', "CL_CreateMove 0x190150 static oldangles: stored from the cmd viewangles at 1903C7..1903D2, copied back into the cmd at 1903DD..1903F6. Each client\\'s own view angles. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x5D34E0, 0x4, 'player', 'its static-init guard (test al,1 at 190158; or at 19015C). Nothing else is initialised under it. It goes with 0x5D34D4. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5D34E4, 0x4, 'player', 'HUD_WeaponsPostThink 0x18E430 static lasthealth: read at 18EE92 to choose Killed or Spawn on the local player object 0x3A0AC0 (18EEB2/18EED5), then set from health [ebp+0x13C] (ftol 0x22EB94, store at 18EEE5). Per-player, like 0x3A0AC4. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x5D45C0, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', "facet ids assigned once from the shared counter 0x3A63B4 (inc / store at 18E74..18E7F and 18D74..18D7F). They must share ownership with the counter and the locale\\'s facet table. A per-player copy would start at 0 and take a new id. C++ runtime. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x5EF6A0, 0x100, 'shared-mutable', 'COM_ExplainDisconnection-like 0x3DF70: vsnprintf into 0x42FBF8 (0x400), then a copy of at most 0xFF chars to 0x5EF6A0 (esi=0xFF at 3DF95, dec at 3DFAA). Terminator at [eax] (3DFC1) and at 0x5EF79F (3DFCA); it sets 0x551F9C=1 (3DFD1). The only reader is its own print (3DFDE/3DFE7); grep finds no other access. Disconnect/UI text; ownership does not change behaviour. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CA600, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'net_local_adr (netadr_t: 5 dwords 6D170..6D188, port word at 6CA612 (6D2DC)), set by NET_GetLocalAddress 0x6D150. Read by the server (98D33, 9A524, 9AB5F) and the console status 5E9C4/5EE67. Network layer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CA740, 0x79, 'shared-mutable', 'chat_buffer of Key_Message 0x65B90: [len+0x6CA740] with len 0x551DF4 capped by cmp ecx, 0x78 (65BEF), store at 65BF4, terminator [len+1+0x6CA740] at 65C01 (so index <= 0x78). Cleared at 65BB0/65C4B; also 0x65ED0. Keyboard chat entry of the one key handler; it goes with 0x551DF0. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CAFE0, None, 'shared-mutable', "keydown[] of Key_Event 0x66510 ([ebp*4+0x6CAFE0] = down at 6653A; ebp is the caller\\'s key number, not bounded here). The engine\\'s one keyboard state (bindings 0x6CABE0 next to it). Extent unproven, ownership only. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x6CDBE0, None, 'shared-mutable', 'key_repeats[] of the same function (66576, 6657F/6658A). Same reasoning. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE1A0, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'targa_header of LoadTGA 0x57810 (callers 0x4E810, R_LoadSkys 0x57E50, 0x58008, 0xB4260). Every field is stored from the file before use: 6CE1A0/A1/A2 bytes, A4/A6 words, A8 byte, AA/AC/AE/B0 words, B2/B3 bytes. The last field is the byte at 0x6CE1B3. No other function accesses it. Scratch. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE1F8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'gldepthmin. R_Clear 0x4E4C0 (gl=5) stores constants (4E555, 4E591) and reads it for the depth range (4E5B3). Read by R_DrawViewModel 0x4D300 (4D3CA..4D5E3) and 0x51900. Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE200, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'gldepthmax, same function (4E4FC..4E587, read at 4E5A6). Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE260, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'scr_vrect and siblings, written by SCR_CalcRefdef 0x55850 (55930..5595B; callers SCR_UpdateScreen 0x55E10 and the view 0xB4560). Read by 0x56180 and 0x65130 (from the view). Display state of the one screen. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE280, 0x4, 'player', "scr_centertime_off. SCR_CenterPrint 0x55180 sets it from scr_centertime 0x37768C (551E9). 0x55180 is called from the client message handlers 0x30A70 (svc_centerprint), 0x31060, 0x31090 and 0x1C5B0. The draw 0x55790 counts it down (5580E/5581A). SCR_BeginLoadingPlaque 55CDB and SV_SpawnServer A001A zero it. Each client\\'s own messages, like 0x551CCC/0x551CD0 [review 32]. It must share ownership with scr_centerstring 0x551CD8 (0x80: strncpy count 0x7F at 551CB) and 0x551CC4/0x551CC8. If shared, player 2\\'s centre prints would show on player 1\\'s screen. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x6CE284, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'same function (558AA/558B2). No reader in this range. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE28C, 0x4, 'player', 'scr_centertime_start = cl.time 0x74A290 (fld at 551D8, fstp at 551E3); read by the draw 0x552B0 (552C4). Same ownership as 0x6CE280. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE2A0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'V_RenderView 0xB5E90 stereo pass: shifts an x offset by half the width (B6103/B610D) and restores it (B6184/B619E). No other accessor. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE2B8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the width that pass halves and restores (B608A/B6098, B6179/B61AA). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE2C4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'a float scaled and restored in the same pass (B6084/B609E, B617E/B6196). Drawing only, net unchanged. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6CE408, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'a screen/timing float. Zeroed by SCR_BeginLoadingPlaque 0x55CB0 (55CE5). Read by the timedemo sampler 0x22170 (221B6; Host_Frame side, like 0x7D67E0) and by 0x65130 from the view (65155). No other statically visible writer. Screen state, same caveat as 0x6CE278. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6D5940, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'current model vertex base, set by GL_BuildLightmaps 0x529C0 from the model [eax+0x94] (52A73, 52B45). Read by BuildSurfaceDisplayList 0x525B0. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6D5960, 0x200, 'shared-mutable', 'lightmap_polys[128]: indexed by surf->lightmaptexturenum [ebp+0x38] (51469/5147C in 0x513C0). R_BlendLightmaps reads esi 0..0x7F (51130; bound cmp esi,0x80 at 51316, reviewed). Cleared by rep stosd in 0x51900 and 0x521B0. Renderer per-view scratch. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6D5B60, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'counter in 0x525B0 (52956..52965). Lightmap build. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6D5B80, 0x10000, 'shared-mutable', 'allocated[] of AllocBlock 0x524A0: mov eax, 0x6D5B80; mov ecx, 0x4000; rep stosd at 529D0..529DE in GL_BuildLightmaps. The lightmap pages are one set for the shared world. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E6380, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'lightmap_bytes = 4 (52A27). Read by the world draw 50420 (50603), R_BlendLightmaps 51181, 513C0 (5150D) and 529C0. Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E77E0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'currentmodel during GL_BuildLightmaps (52A81, 52B4B, 52E39), read by 0x525B0 (525B8/52609). Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E77E4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'skytexturenum, set by R_NewMap 0x4F8D0 (-1 at 4F97A, found at 4F9F2), read by the world draw 0x51630 (516CC). Renderer world state. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7A04, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'lightmap_textures: allocated once from texture_extension_number 0x377788 (+0x80) only while zero (529E0..52A05). It must share ownership with the GL texture numbers: a per-player copy would allocate a second range of 128 textures. Read by the world, studio and decal draw (505BB, 5113F, 54D21, 195B9D, 196B3D...). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7A08, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'the lightmap format/bytes (52A2D/52A3A). Renderer. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7A24, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', "fields of r_refdef 0x6E7A20 (vrect), written by SCR_CalcRefdef 0x55850, V_RenderView\\'s setup 0xB5D10, V_RenderView 0xB5E90 (B619C/B61A4) and the envmap command 0x4F330. Same evidence as the reviewed 0x6E7A20. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x6E7AA0, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'r_refdef.viewangles[1..2], after 0x6E7A9C (viewangles[0], reviewed). Set by 0xB5D10, adjusted by 0xB5E90 (B60A4..B6126) and the envmap command 0x4F330/0x4FA70. Per-view scratch. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7AAC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'r_refdef field set by 0xB5D10 and tested by V_RenderView (B604E). Per-view scratch. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7B00, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'lighting ints of R_DrawViewModel 0x4D300 (gl=3): 4D4FE/4D504, then 4D56D..4D5B6. Drawing only. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7B14, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'same function (4D5C0). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7FA0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'r_framecount: R_SetupFrame 0x4DC00 increments it (4DE1A/4DE36); GL_BuildLightmaps sets 1 (529EE). Read only by renderer code (4B4F5, 4B7A9, 4BA25, 4FFC5, 514E6, 52062, 8F373, 8FB11, 92BD4). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7FA4, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'currententity. Written by the draw functions (R_DrawViewModel 0x4D300, 0x4D650, 0x51900, R_DrawEntitiesOnList 0x4D0D0, 0x51630, 0x521B0, R_DrawTransEntities 0x93600). The one writer reached from the client frame, 0x8CAF0 (<- 0x92430 <- CL_EmitEntities side 0x24FE0), saves it (8CAFC), sets it (8CB2D) and restores it (8CB40): no net change. Renderer scratch. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E7FBC, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'a shading float written by the entity draw 0x4CBD0 (gl=12; 4CE21) and read by 0x4CB00 / 0x4CBD0. Drawing only. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E8000, 0xC, 'shared-mutable', 'a vec3 written by the entity draw 0x4CBD0 (4CBD0/4CC3A entries), 0x51900 (gl=11) and 0x521B0 (gl=8), all from R_RenderView 0x4EC60. Three exact dwords. Drawing scratch. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E872C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'set by R_NewMap 0x4F8D0 (4F917), read by R_RenderView 0x4EF00 (4EF1D). Renderer world state. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E8774, 0x8, 'shared-mutable', 'set by the entity draw code only: 0x4CBD0 (4CBD0/4CC3A entries), R_DrawEntitiesOnList 0x4D0D0, the sprite pass 0x93600. Drawing. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E877C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'mirrortexturenum: R_NewMap (-1 at 4F984, found at 4FA1F); read by 0x51630 (516DD) and 0x51F40 (520BF). Renderer world state. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E8824, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'a polygon counter: R_RenderView 0x4EF00 zeroes it (4EF60) and prints it ("%4i wpoly %4i epoly", 4F025). 0x513C0 increments it (513C0/513D1); R_SetupFrame 4DF41. Renderer statistics. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E889C, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'an ambient/shade float of the entity draw 0x4CBD0 (constants at 4CCE1/4CD7E/4CDF4, fstp at 4CD58). Drawing. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E88A0, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'set by 0x4CB00 (4CB10), called only from 0x4CBD0. Drawing. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x6E88A8, 0x14, 'shared-mutable', 'lightplane 0x6E88A8 (4BC46) and lightspot 0x6E88B0..0x6E88B8 (4BC29/4BC35/4BC3A) of RecursiveLightPoint 0x4BA90 (<- R_LightPoint 0x4BE50 <- the view model and studio lighting 0x4BF10, 0x8FDA0, 0x90013). Written per call; who.py finds no reader. 0x6E88AC (r_dlightframecount-like) is set by 0x4B790 (from R_RenderView, 4B7B4) and 0x4BA10 (only from V_RenderView, 4BA2D), and read by R_MarkLights 0x4B870 (4B9A0). Drawing only. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x748740, 0xB4C, 'player', "a local_state_t: mov ecx, 0x2D3; rep stosd at 33A5A/33A5F, the same size as the frame local state (imul eax, 0xB4C at 23FB0). 0x33A50 (from the per-connect 0x2D350) clears it and initialises it with this player\\'s cl.playernum 0x771224 (33ACD..33B06) when cls 0x78578C is set. 0x33B10 runs movement on it with cl.cmd 0x74A0EC and copies the result into cl 0x74A144.. (33B65..33BE5). 0x33B10 is called from Host_Frame at 5D504, inside the player\\'s client half. CL_ParseClientdata uses it as from/to (23F68..23F7A). Every accessor is the player\\'s own client code with its own cl/cls. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x7492C0, 0x8, 'player', "double: the sent time of the acknowledged frame (fld [edx+0x7658D4]; fstp at 23EFB/23F01), subtracted from realtime 0x6CE040 to give cls.latency (24019/24023). Each client\\'s own frames. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x749C20, 0x100, 'shared-mutable', 'per-svc byte counts of one message. CL_ParseServerMessage 0x30260 clears them at the start of every message (rep stosd at 302CF). It adds to [esi*4+0x749C20] (30480/30490; esi < 0x40 by cmp esi,0x3F at 3043A). At the end of the same call (30601) it calls 0x2FF50, which folds them into the per-player 0x749B20 (loop bound 0x100 at 2FFA2/2FFA5). Scratch: cleared and consumed inside one call, never across a context switch. A per-player copy is equally correct. [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x785B9C, 0x4, 'player', "connect-handshake length after cls: set to -1 by CL_ConnectionlessPacket 0x27CE0 (27E28, 27F11, just before calling 0x29310 at 27F1D). Read by the connect-packet builder 0x29310 (2950F cmp 0x320; 29716, len+it < 0x800). 0x27CE0 is called from CL_ReadPackets 0x28A40. Each client\\'s own connection. [review 2/ut_63]"),
    (0x785BA8, 0x4, 'shared-mutable', 'write-only: the only access is 2849C (mov [0x785BA8], [esi+0x44] in the resource code 0x282E0); grep finds no reader. Ownership does not change behaviour (as with 0x552B9D). [review 2/ut_63]'),
    (0x7863E0, 0x1100, 'player', 'cl_lightstyle[64] x 0x44. svc_lightstyle 0x30C90 reads the index from net_message, errors if >= 0x40 (30CBF), and writes stride 0x44 (imul edx,edx,0x44 at 30CE4): string at +4 (30CE9, <= 0x3F chars), terminator at 30D0E, length at +0 (30D2B). CL_ClearState clears it (mov ecx, 0x440; rep stosd at 28ECE/28EDF). Read by the shared R_AnimateLight (4B570/4B587). [review 2/ut_63]'),
